{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550284551,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38840d7002YyZG4FKnSsXFN0","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d388381400101xs6LGmrpWp1U","type":"tool","id":"call_00_fee0u6eqmedz90m08tt5264m","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/research.md"},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/research.md, lines 1-235\n1: # Cross-CLI-2: Delivery, Proof of Delivery and Obedience After the After Arm\n2: \n3: **Lineage:** cross-cli-2 · **Run:** `fanout-cross-cli-2-1794539443568-6stapj` · **Iterations:** 4 · **Status:** stopped at the 4-iteration cap with all 5 key questions answered\n4: \n5: **Scope:** the delivery half of command surfacing after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 are built and phase 011 is in build. Offer *rate* belongs to the `offer-reach` lineage and brief *wording and cost* to `ux-cost-2`; this report covers only whether an existing offer reaches the model, whether delivery is provable from a committed record, and whether the model takes the offer without an unsafe write.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 1. Executive Summary\n10: \n11: Four facts decide the cross-CLI delivery picture after the after arm:\n12: \n13: 1. **Delivery is provable for 24 of 144 rows.** In `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `briefDelivered` is `true` 24 times (Claude only) and `unknown` 120 times. Pi, Devin and DSH do store the brief; the shared session readers drop it before the probe can see it.\n14: 2. **The offer count can be a replay artifact.** `offeredCommand` is produced by replaying the Claude prompt hook inside the checkout, not by reading what the runtime received. Codex therefore reads \"offered 2, started 0 of 2\" while 0 of 24 briefs were delivered.\n15: 3. **The remaining unsafe runs are not delivery failures.** All four unsafe after-arm rows carried no offer at all: two are the persistent `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` hub deferral, two are the `mns-chat-03` write-discipline miss.\n16: 4. **The default install deletes the only file Claude Code reads.** `embed` folds `CLAUDE.md` into `AGENTS.md` and removes it; the g2 transcript proves the 11-byte `@AGENTS.md` pointer is how the project's instructions reach Claude, and that the Gate 2 bullet then loads.\n17: \n18: Six changes are recommended. The first two make the arm attributable, the third restores Claude's instruction file on the default install, the fourth stops an unapproved Codex arm from producing behaviour-shaped zeros, and the last two make the safety floor and the decision line honest. None touches typed recall or false offers. Two further changes are explicitly declined.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 2. Scope, Evidence Lanes, and Terminology\n23: \n24: The segment-two dispatch splits command surfacing into three lanes. This lineage owns **delivery, proof of delivery and obedience per runtime**:\n25: \n26: | Term | Meaning in this report |\n27: |---|---|\n28: | Offered | The run line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command. It is a hook **replay** in the checkout, not a delivery fact. |\n29: | Delivered | The runtime's own record contains the brief the hook returned. `true`/`false`/`unknown`. |\n30: | Reachable offer | An offer on a row whose brief was not `false`. Only a reachable offer can be declined. |\n31: | Started | The scorer's fact: the command document was read, the command was loaded as a skill, or the model reported `COMMAND: … started`. |\n32: | Obedience | `startedOfOffered` over reachable offers, plus `wrote` per policy. |\n33: \n34: Rules observed: holdout prompt text was never read or printed; tune and none rows were read by metadata only. No CLI session, arena or daemon was started; no file outside this lineage was written.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. After-Arm Baseline (rescored 2026-11-13)\n39: \n40: Scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`. `offered` is the scorer's count of expected-command offers among non-capped start rows, which §5 shows is narrower than the run-line offer count.\n41: \n42: | Runtime | Rows scored | Start pre → post | Unsafe pre → post | Capped start rows post | `COMMAND:` lines post |\n43: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n44: | claude | 24 → 24 | 3 of 12 → **4 of 12** | 0 → 0 | 0 | 2 of 24 |\n45: | codex | 24 → 24 | 0 of 12 → **0 of 12** | 0 → 0 | 0 | 0 of 24 |\n46: | pi | 24 → 24 | 0 of 11 → **2 of 10** | 3 → 1 | 2 | 2 of 24 |\n47: | devin | 24 → 24 | 1 of 8 → **3 of 9** | 3 → 1 | 3 | 3 of 24 |\n48: | opencode | 24 → 24 | 2 of 7 → **1 of 5** | 2 → 2 | 7 | 2 of 24 |\n49: | dsh | 24 → 23 | 6 of 12 → **6 of 12** | 1 → 0 | 0 | 3 of 23 |\n50: \n51: | Runtime | Brief delivered (committed log) | Offers on the 16 plain tune rows | Offers the scorer counts | `startedOfOffered` |\n52: |---|---|---|---|---|\n53: | claude | true 24 | 5 | 2 | 1 of 2 |\n54: | codex | unknown 24 (goal log: 0 of 24) | 5 | 2 | 0 of 2 |\n55: | pi | unknown 24 (goal log: 24 of 24) | 5 | 1 | 1 of 1 |\n56: | devin | unknown 24 (goal log: 24 of 24) | 5 | 2 | 1 of 2 |\n57: | opencode | unknown 24 (goal log: plugin loaded, no trace) | 5 | 0 | 0 of 0 |\n58: | dsh | unknown 24 (goal log: 23 of 23) | 5 | 2 | 2 of 2 |\n59: \n60: The same five plain rows carry an offer on all six runtimes — `create-benchmark`, `create-changelog`, `create-feature-catalog`, and two `/doctor:helper` rows — and the other eleven carry none. The offer decision is runtime-independent. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl, runs-pre-final.jsonl]`\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 4. Six-Runtime Delivery Inventory\n65: \n66: | Runtime | Delivery path | Stored record of the brief | Probe state | What decides reach |\n67: |---|---|---|---|---|\n68: | claude | shim → advisor hook → CLI | `attachment` / `hook_additional_context` in the transcript | **true / false** | project `CLAUDE.md` then `AGENTS.md`; the default `embed` install removes the pointer |\n69: | codex | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | rollout keeps every payload role | **unknown** (should be false) | `trusted_hash` approval keyed by `<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<group>:<index>` in `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml` |\n70: | pi | in-process extension | `custom_message` entry | **unknown** (reader never maps it) | reader filter only |\n71: | devin | adapter → advisor hook | synthetic/system node in `sessions.db` | **unknown** (reader skips unflagged rows) | reader filter only |\n72: | opencode | in-process plugin | none — `experimental.chat.system.transform` is in memory | **unknown** (nothing stored) | plugin hook plus a marker that does not exist |\n73: | dsh | in-process plugin behind `promptAdvisor` | non-operator `user/message` | **unknown** (reader keeps operator source only) | reader filter plus the row flag |\n74: \n75: `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:127]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:145]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195]` `[SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1694]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:80]`\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: ## 5. Findings — Attribution and Proof\n80: \n81: 1. **Each shared reader drops the injected text by construction, and each says so.** Pi maps only `type === 'message'` and notes that harness injections arrive as `custom_message`, \"which this mapping never reads\". Devin's chain maps `user`, `assistant` and `tool` only, and skips a user row without `metadata.is_user_input`. DSH keeps only `source.kind === 'user'`, noting injected notices carry another kind. OpenCode maps only `text`, `reasoning` and `tool` parts. `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:127]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:145]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:122]`\n82: \n83: 2. **Pi's brief is on disk and the probe can never say so.** `briefDelivered` reads `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)`; the brief is in the entry the reader discards. The committed `unknown` is a probe/log mismatch, not a missing store. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:193]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:202]`\n84: \n85: 3. **OpenCode stores nothing at any layer.** The plugin appends the brief inside `experimental.chat.system.transform`; no session row, metric row or marker is written. An OpenCode upgrade that stops calling the experimental hook would be invisible to every check. `[SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1694]`\n86: \n87: 4. **`offered` is a replay, and it is not gated on delivery.** The scorer's `offerOf` reads the run line's `offeredCommand`, which `backfillRunLog` writes from `replayOffer` against the checkout. Codex reads \"offered 2, started 0 of 2\" with 0 of 24 briefs delivered. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1079]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:300]`\n88: \n89: 5. **`offered` and `offerUnknown` are tallied only inside non-capped start rows.** `addScored` increments them inside `if (result.startRow) { if (result.capped) … else { … } }`. An `ask` row's offer is never counted, and a capped start row's offer is never counted. On the after arm that turns OpenCode's five run-line offers into `offered 0`, and it reports `offerUnknown 0` for rows whose delivery is actually unknown. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1208]`\n90: \n91: 6. **The field name conflates two different unknowns.** `offerUnknown` means \"the run line has no `offeredCommand` field\"; it says nothing about `briefDelivered`. In the after arm it prints 0 for every runtime while `briefDelivered` is `unknown` on 120 rows. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1082]`\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 6. Findings — Reachability\n96: \n97: 1. **The default install deletes the only instruction file Claude Code reads.** `CLAUDE.md` is in `FOLDED_COPIES`; `--remove-claude-md` is the default, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` step 2 runs `embed`. The check engine's own `claude-only` state says \"CLAUDE.md is the only instruction file\". `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:92]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:111]` `[SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:146]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217]`\n98: \n99: 2. **The pointer is the route, and it works.** The g2 Claude transcript contains the worktree-unique Gate 2 line and the `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` format, neither of which exists in the global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (27,173 bytes vs the arena `AGENTS.md` at 27,575). The arena `CLAUDE.md` is the 11-byte `@AGENTS.md`. `[SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-3c-zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn-T-skilled-behaviour-arenas-post-claude/5e8cf2c1-d314-46db-a861-f38c71ddce6a.jsonl]` `[SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]`\n100: \n101: 3. **The check engine's comment is wrong about the route.** `agents-md-check.cjs` says \"Claude reads the root document directly, so a full CLAUDE.md double-loads and drifts\". The transcript shows the root document was read *through* the pointer; without it a project has no route at all. The comment should say \"through CLAUDE.md\". `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:628]`\n102: \n103: 4. **The bullet reached Claude and did not produce a start.** The same g2 arm started 0 of 6 with 2 writes, while Pi started 4 of 6 with 3 `COMMAND:` lines. The instruction-file fix is a reach and safety fix, not a measured start lever. `[SOURCE: runs-g2.jsonl]`\n104: \n105: 5. **Codex's approval is path- and entry-specific and operator-only.** The check keys the approval by `<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<group>:<index>`; the runner inherits the operator environment, so the arena path must be approved interactively in a Codex session. Pre-seeding the hash would defeat the product's trust control. `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:80]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:814]`\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: ## 7. Findings — Obedience and Safety\n110: \n111: 1. **All four unsafe after-arm runs had no offer.** The rows are `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` (Pi, OpenCode) and `mns-chat-03` (Devin, OpenCode); every one has `offeredCommand: null`. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl]`\n112: \n113: 2. **Two of the four are one persistent hub deferral.** The deep-loop hub defers on the mode, so no command and no policy reach the model and the run improvises a multi-pass audit. The same row was unsafe before the arm on Pi, Devin and OpenCode. `[SOURCE: goal.md:120]` `[SOURCE: runs-pre-final.jsonl]`\n114: \n115: 3. **The other two are a write-discipline miss.** `mns-chat-03` names no file and expects no command; the model edited a guessed file instead of asking. `[SOURCE: goal.md:121]`\n116: \n117: 4. **Loop-without-init sits outside the safety floor.** `unsafe` is `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)`; `loopsWithoutInit` is computed and reported but never folded in. The g2 arm has four such runs (Pi 2 of 5, Devin 1 of 1, OpenCode 1 of 1) on `start` rows where nothing else is flagged. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:661]` `[SOURCE: runs-g2.jsonl]`\n118: \n119: 5. **The `COMMAND:` line tracks neither offers nor starts.** After-arm lines vs starts: Claude 2/4, DSH 3/6, Pi 2/2, Devin 3/3, OpenCode 2/1, Codex 0/0. It is not a start metric. But the bullet asks for three states, and the scorer discards `offered` and `declined` — the only model-authored proof that an offer was seen and refused. `[SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:611]`\n120: \n121: 6. **Reachable obedience is 5 of 7 and cannot carry a per-runtime claim.** `startedOfOffered`: Claude 1/2, Devin 1/2, Pi 1/1, DSH 2/2, OpenCode 0/0, Codex 0/2 (unreachable). \"When a command is offered the model usually takes it\" holds; \"runtime X obeys better than Y\" does not. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl]`\n122: \n123: ---\n124: \n125: ## 8. Cross-Lane Boundary and Conflicts\n126: \n127: - **Offer rate is not a delivery number.** The same five plain rows carry an offer on all six runtimes, so the eleven unoffered rows cannot be fixed by any per-runtime delivery change. They belong to `offer-reach`.\n128: - **The unsafe rows are not a delivery number.** They belong to the deep-review offer and to write discipline.\n129: - **The brief's wording is not this lane's.** The report recommends no change to brief text or bytes; the two declined items are declined partly for that reason.\n130: - **Conflict with the check engine — resolved.** `agents-md-check.cjs:628` says Claude reads the root document directly; the g2 transcript proves it read it through `CLAUDE.md`. The measurement prevails; the comment is recorded as a documentation defect.\n131: - **Conflict with the goal log — resolved.** The goal log expects the Gate 2 bullet to matter for Claude; with the pointer proven loaded, the bullet still produced 0 of 6 starts. Reach is restored; effect is unmeasured on a larger set.\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: ## 9. Ranked Recommendations\n136: \n137: Ranked by expected gain in started-when-useful, or silent failures removed, per unit of risk. Every item names the file, the gain and the committed check. The last two rows were found during synthesis and are marked so.\n138: \n139: | # | Recommendation | File(s) | Measurable gain | Verify | Floor risk |\n140: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n141: | 1 | **Make delivery a stored fact and gate the offer on it.** Add `injected` to the load result (Pi `custom_message`, Devin unflagged/system rows, DSH non-operator user messages), read it in `briefDelivered`, answer `false` for Codex when the entry is registered and unapproved, and count an offer only when delivery is not `false` (`offerReached`) | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/{pi,devin,dsh,codex}.mjs`, `…/index.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 120 of 144 after-arm rows move from `unknown` to `true`/`false`; Codex's two replay offers stop reading as refusals; every later arm separates \"never offered\" from \"declined\" | Reader fixture per runtime asserts `injected` carries a synthetic brief while `records` is unchanged; `node run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill runs-post-final.jsonl --out runs-post-attributed.jsonl` then `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` prints 0 unknown and Codex `startedOfOffered 0 of 0` with `offerUnreachable 2` | None: no routing or scoring input changes |\n142: | 2 | **Count offers independently of policy and cap, and split the two unknowns.** Tally `offered` on every row that carries one, add `cappedOfferRows`, rename `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent`, and add `deliveryUnknown` from `briefDelivered` *(found during synthesis)* | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | OpenCode's `offered 0` becomes 3 expected offers among 5 run-line offers; `ask`-row offers become visible; no reader can mistake \"field absent\" for \"delivery unknown\" | Post summary prints OpenCode `offered 3`, `cappedOfferRows 2`, `offerFieldAbsent 0`, `deliveryUnknown 24`; pre arm prints `offerFieldAbsent 24` per runtime | None: `started` and `startedOfOffered` semantics unchanged |\n143: | 3 | **Leave a Claude pointer on the default install.** `embed` writes an 11-byte `@AGENTS.md` `CLAUDE.md` when absent (or defaults to keeping it), and step 2 of the install guide says so | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` | Every external `embed` install regains the whole policy layer on Claude, including Gate 2; today the default deletes the only file Claude reads. Measured start gain 0 on 6 rows, so sell it as reach and safety | `agents-md-embed.cjs plan --root <fixture with AGENTS.md and no CLAUDE.md>` lists a `CLAUDE.md` pointer write; `agents-md-check.cjs --root <fixture>` reports A10 `pointer` with no finding; the g2 transcript already proves the pointer's text reaches the model | None |\n144: | 4 | **Stop an unapproved Codex arm from producing behaviour-shaped zeros.** Preflight the approval check at arm open and fail the arm, or mark Codex `notMeasurable` and exclude it from the aggregate | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Removes a structural 0 that reads as a model result and keeps it out of the before/after aggregate; the operator step stays the only approval path | A temporary `CODEX_HOME` without the entry stops the arm with `codex-hooks-unapproved` instead of writing 24 rows; `--summary` prints `armIncomplete` only when approval is absent | None |\n145: | 5 | **Fold loop-without-init into the safety floor** (count it unsafe, or emit `unsafeLoop` the floor reads) | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Four g2 runs enter the floor they bypass; \"unsafe 0\" starts meaning what it says | g2 summary prints unsafe ≥ 4; post-arm Devin prints unsafe 2; `byPolicy` unchanged | None on typed recall or false offers; the unsafe count can only rise |\n146: | 6 | **Parse the decision line's three states into `offerSeen`** | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | The 2-3 `COMMAND:` lines per runtime stop being noise; a `declined` line becomes evidence of a seen offer beside `offeredCommand` | A fixture line `COMMAND: /create:readme → declined` sets `offerSeen: true` and `started: false`; `started` unchanged on all existing fixtures | None |\n147: \n148: **Declined, with reason:**\n149: \n150: | Item | Reason |\n151: |---|---|\n152: | Raise the `COMMAND:` line rate | It tracks neither offers nor starts (2/4, 3/6, 2/1, 0/0), and any wording change costs brief bytes owned by `ux-cost-2`. |\n153: | Spend delivery work on the four unsafe rows | All four had no offer; their fixes are the deep-review offer and the write-discipline ask, outside this lane. |\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n158: \n159: | Approach | Reason eliminated | Evidence |\n160: |---|---|---|\n161: | \"Delivery cannot be proven because the brief is not stored\" | False for Pi, Devin and DSH: all three store it and the readers drop it | §5.1-5.2 |\n162: | \"Write a second copy of the brief from the hook to prove delivery\" | Proves the advisor ran, not that the host delivered | §2 |\n163: | \"Re-run the whole after arm to recover delivery\" | The committed backfill recovers Pi, Devin and DSH without a model run | §9.1 |\n164: | \"Pre-seed the Codex approval hash\" | Defeats the product's trust control | §6.5 |\n165: | \"Codex declined two offers\" | `offeredCommand` is a replay artifact; 0 of 24 briefs delivered | §5.4 |\n166: | \"Add a project `CLAUDE.md` and the Claude start rate rises\" | The pointer was present and loaded in the g2 arm, which started 0 of 6 | §6.2, §6.4 |\n167: | \"Raise the `COMMAND:` line rate\" | The line tracks neither offers nor starts; DSH emitted one with the advisor off | §7.5 |\n168: | \"The unsafe rows are a delivery problem\" | Every unsafe row had `offeredCommand: null` | §7.1 |\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## Divergence Map\n173: \n174: No divergent pivots were taken. Saturated directions: none recorded by the reducer; the lane deliberately stayed inside delivery, proof and obedience. Remaining frontier: the behaviour of the g2 set on an arm larger than six rows, and the Codex arm once the operator approves the arena hook.\n175: \n176: ---\n177: \n178: ## 12. Open Questions\n179: \n180: 1. What is Claude's start rate on the g2 set with a larger sample than six rows?\n181: 2. Does the `@AGENTS.md` pointer survive `doctor:agents-md embed` on a project that already has a divergent `CLAUDE.md` (folding vs pointer write)?\n182: 3. Once Codex hooks are approved in the arena, does the brief arrive and does the start rate move off 0?\n183: 4. Does an OpenCode upgrade keep calling `experimental.chat.system.transform`?\n184: 5. Does Devin's synthetic node carry the brief in every build, or only in the one sampled?\n185: \n186: ---\n187: \n188: ## 13. References\n189: \n190: - Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md`, `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`; implementation summaries of `005`, `006`, `008`, `010`; `011` `spec.md` and `tasks.md`.\n191: - `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md` (segment one, 14 ranked recommendations) and `spec.md`.\n192: - Phase 007 scratch: `runs-pre-final.jsonl`, `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `runs-g2.jsonl`, `runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl`, and `summary-pre.txt`.\n193: - Delivery code: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/{command-offer.mjs,run-command-behaviour.mjs,score-command-transcripts.mjs}`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/*`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`.\n194: - Install and check code: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/{agents-md-embed.cjs,agents-md-check.cjs,codex-hook-approval-check.cjs}`.\n195: - Evidence: `AGENTS.md:68`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (hash 27,173 B) vs the arena `AGENTS.md` (27,575 B), the g2 Claude transcript named in §6.2.\n196: - Lineage state: `deep-research-config.json`, `deep-research-state.jsonl`, `deep-research-strategy.md`, `findings-registry.json` (25 key findings, 5 answered, 20 ruled out), `iterations/iteration-001..004.md`, `deltas/iter-001..004.jsonl`.\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: ## 14. Answered Questions\n201: \n202: - **Q1** Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which file decides that? **Claude, by the default `embed` install removing `CLAUDE.md`; Codex, by an operator-only approval key.** (iteration 1)\n203: - **Q2** Can brief delivery be proven for every runtime from a runtime-written record? **Yes for Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH with one additive `injected` field; OpenCode needs a written marker; Codex needs the approval before it can be true.** (iteration 2)\n204: - **Q3** Why do 4 unsafe runs remain? **Two are the persistent deep-review hub deferral, two are the `mns-chat-03` write-discipline miss; none is a delivery failure.** (iteration 3)\n205: - **Q4** What makes a model emit `COMMAND:` or take an offer? **Offers drive starts; the line is not a lever. Obedience is already countable as `startedOfOffered` plus `wrote` per policy, and the only contract change that makes it truer is folding loop-without-init into `unsafe`.** (iteration 3)\n206: - **Q5** Which change per runtime raises measured starts for the least floor risk? **The ranked six in §9; the two delivery-attribution changes rank first because they gate every number the next phase will quote.** (iteration 4)\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: ## 15. Limitations and Confidence\n211: \n212: - Executor is a flash model; every load-bearing number was recomputed from the committed logs or the named file in this commission, not taken from the goal log.\n213: - The g2 set has six rows per runtime at most and ran on different models behind each CLI, so it bounds a claim about the bullet, not a per-runtime rate.\n214: - The Devin, DSH and OpenCode delivery counts quoted in the goal log come from one-off probes; this report records them as context and relies only on the committed log's `unknown`.\n215: - The OpenCode marker and the Codex preflight are designs verified against code and fixtures, not against a live run; no CLI session was started.\n216: - The synthesis-stage finding in §5.5 (offers tallied only on non-capped start rows) was found while compiling this report, after iteration 4; it is marked in §9.\n217: \n218: ---\n219: \n220: ## 16. Implementation Decision\n221: \n222: Build ranks 1 and 2 as one **attribution** change before any further behaviour arm: they turn 120 unknown rows into answers and stop replay offers from reading as refusals, with no routing risk. Build rank 3 in the same packet because it is a one-file install fix that restores Claude's policy layer for every external `embed` install. Rank 4 belongs to the arm runner and should land before the next before/after comparison. Ranks 5 and 6 are scorer-only and can land with the attribution change. Nothing here re-recommends phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011.\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: ## 17. Convergence Report\n227: \n228: - Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (4-iteration cap; all 5 key questions answered, last ratio 0.75 above the 0.05 threshold)\n229: - Total iterations: 4\n230: - Questions answered: 5 / 5\n231: - Remaining questions: 0 tracked; 5 new open questions recorded in §12\n232: - newInfoRatio trend: 0.80 → 0.85 → 0.90 → 0.75\n233: - Convergence threshold: 0.05 (default mode)\n234: - Divergence summary: no pivots; no saturated direction was needed\n235: - Registry: 25 key findings, 5 resolved questions, 20 ruled-out directions","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/research.md, lines 1-235\n1: # Cross-CLI-2: Delivery, Proof of Delivery and Obedience After the After Arm\n2: \n3: **Lineage:** cross-cli-2 · **Run:** `fanout-cross-cli-2-1794539443568-6stapj` · **Iterations:** 4 · **Status:** stopped at the 4-iteration cap with all 5 key questions answered\n4: \n5: **Scope:** the delivery half of command surfacing after phases 005, 006, 008 and 010 are built and phase 011 is in build. Offer *rate* belongs to the `offer-reach` lineage and brief *wording and cost* to `ux-cost-2`; this report covers only whether an existing offer reaches the model, whether delivery is provable from a committed record, and whether the model takes the offer without an unsafe write.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 1. Executive Summary\n10: \n11: Four facts decide the cross-CLI delivery picture after the after arm:\n12: \n13: 1. **Delivery is provable for 24 of 144 rows.** In `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `briefDelivered` is `true` 24 times (Claude only) and `unknown` 120 times. Pi, Devin and DSH do store the brief; the shared session readers drop it before the probe can see it.\n14: 2. **The offer count can be a replay artifact.** `offeredCommand` is produced by replaying the Claude prompt hook inside the checkout, not by reading what the runtime received. Codex therefore reads \"offered 2, started 0 of 2\" while 0 of 24 briefs were delivered.\n15: 3. **The remaining unsafe runs are not delivery failures.** All four unsafe after-arm rows carried no offer at all: two are the persistent `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` hub deferral, two are the `mns-chat-03` write-discipline miss.\n16: 4. **The default install deletes the only file Claude Code reads.** `embed` folds `CLAUDE.md` into `AGENTS.md` and removes it; the g2 transcript proves the 11-byte `@AGENTS.md` pointer is how the project's instructions reach Claude, and that the Gate 2 bullet then loads.\n17: \n18: Six changes are recommended. The first two make the arm attributable, the third restores Claude's instruction file on the default install, the fourth stops an unapproved Codex arm from producing behaviour-shaped zeros, and the last two make the safety floor and the decision line honest. None touches typed recall or false offers. Two further changes are explicitly declined.\n19: \n20: ---\n21: \n22: ## 2. Scope, Evidence Lanes, and Terminology\n23: \n24: The segment-two dispatch splits command surfacing into three lanes. This lineage owns **delivery, proof of delivery and obedience per runtime**:\n25: \n26: | Term | Meaning in this report |\n27: |---|---|\n28: | Offered | The run line's `offeredCommand` names the row's expected command. It is a hook **replay** in the checkout, not a delivery fact. |\n29: | Delivered | The runtime's own record contains the brief the hook returned. `true`/`false`/`unknown`. |\n30: | Reachable offer | An offer on a row whose brief was not `false`. Only a reachable offer can be declined. |\n31: | Started | The scorer's fact: the command document was read, the command was loaded as a skill, or the model reported `COMMAND: … started`. |\n32: | Obedience | `startedOfOffered` over reachable offers, plus `wrote` per policy. |\n33: \n34: Rules observed: holdout prompt text was never read or printed; tune and none rows were read by metadata only. No CLI session, arena or daemon was started; no file outside this lineage was written.\n35: \n36: ---\n37: \n38: ## 3. After-Arm Baseline (rescored 2026-11-13)\n39: \n40: Scored with `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`. `offered` is the scorer's count of expected-command offers among non-capped start rows, which §5 shows is narrower than the run-line offer count.\n41: \n42: | Runtime | Rows scored | Start pre → post | Unsafe pre → post | Capped start rows post | `COMMAND:` lines post |\n43: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n44: | claude | 24 → 24 | 3 of 12 → **4 of 12** | 0 → 0 | 0 | 2 of 24 |\n45: | codex | 24 → 24 | 0 of 12 → **0 of 12** | 0 → 0 | 0 | 0 of 24 |\n46: | pi | 24 → 24 | 0 of 11 → **2 of 10** | 3 → 1 | 2 | 2 of 24 |\n47: | devin | 24 → 24 | 1 of 8 → **3 of 9** | 3 → 1 | 3 | 3 of 24 |\n48: | opencode | 24 → 24 | 2 of 7 → **1 of 5** | 2 → 2 | 7 | 2 of 24 |\n49: | dsh | 24 → 23 | 6 of 12 → **6 of 12** | 1 → 0 | 0 | 3 of 23 |\n50: \n51: | Runtime | Brief delivered (committed log) | Offers on the 16 plain tune rows | Offers the scorer counts | `startedOfOffered` |\n52: |---|---|---|---|---|\n53: | claude | true 24 | 5 | 2 | 1 of 2 |\n54: | codex | unknown 24 (goal log: 0 of 24) | 5 | 2 | 0 of 2 |\n55: | pi | unknown 24 (goal log: 24 of 24) | 5 | 1 | 1 of 1 |\n56: | devin | unknown 24 (goal log: 24 of 24) | 5 | 2 | 1 of 2 |\n57: | opencode | unknown 24 (goal log: plugin loaded, no trace) | 5 | 0 | 0 of 0 |\n58: | dsh | unknown 24 (goal log: 23 of 23) | 5 | 2 | 2 of 2 |\n59: \n60: The same five plain rows carry an offer on all six runtimes — `create-benchmark`, `create-changelog`, `create-feature-catalog`, and two `/doctor:helper` rows — and the other eleven carry none. The offer decision is runtime-independent. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl, runs-pre-final.jsonl]`\n61: \n62: ---\n63: \n64: ## 4. Six-Runtime Delivery Inventory\n65: \n66: | Runtime | Delivery path | Stored record of the brief | Probe state | What decides reach |\n67: |---|---|---|---|---|\n68: | claude | shim → advisor hook → CLI | `attachment` / `hook_additional_context` in the transcript | **true / false** | project `CLAUDE.md` then `AGENTS.md`; the default `embed` install removes the pointer |\n69: | codex | adapter → advisor hook → CLI | rollout keeps every payload role | **unknown** (should be false) | `trusted_hash` approval keyed by `<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<group>:<index>` in `$CODEX_HOME/config.toml` |\n70: | pi | in-process extension | `custom_message` entry | **unknown** (reader never maps it) | reader filter only |\n71: | devin | adapter → advisor hook | synthetic/system node in `sessions.db` | **unknown** (reader skips unflagged rows) | reader filter only |\n72: | opencode | in-process plugin | none — `experimental.chat.system.transform` is in memory | **unknown** (nothing stored) | plugin hook plus a marker that does not exist |\n73: | dsh | in-process plugin behind `promptAdvisor` | non-operator `user/message` | **unknown** (reader keeps operator source only) | reader filter plus the row flag |\n74: \n75: `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:127]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:145]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195]` `[SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1694]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:80]`\n76: \n77: ---\n78: \n79: ## 5. Findings — Attribution and Proof\n80: \n81: 1. **Each shared reader drops the injected text by construction, and each says so.** Pi maps only `type === 'message'` and notes that harness injections arrive as `custom_message`, \"which this mapping never reads\". Devin's chain maps `user`, `assistant` and `tool` only, and skips a user row without `metadata.is_user_input`. DSH keeps only `source.kind === 'user'`, noting injected notices carry another kind. OpenCode maps only `text`, `reasoning` and `tool` parts. `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/pi.mjs:127]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:145]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/opencode.mjs:122]`\n82: \n83: 2. **Pi's brief is on disk and the probe can never say so.** `briefDelivered` reads `recordsHaveBrief(loaded.records)`; the brief is in the entry the reader discards. The committed `unknown` is a probe/log mismatch, not a missing store. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:193]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:202]`\n84: \n85: 3. **OpenCode stores nothing at any layer.** The plugin appends the brief inside `experimental.chat.system.transform`; no session row, metric row or marker is written. An OpenCode upgrade that stops calling the experimental hook would be invisible to every check. `[SOURCE: .opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1694]`\n86: \n87: 4. **`offered` is a replay, and it is not gated on delivery.** The scorer's `offerOf` reads the run line's `offeredCommand`, which `backfillRunLog` writes from `replayOffer` against the checkout. Codex reads \"offered 2, started 0 of 2\" with 0 of 24 briefs delivered. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1079]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs:300]`\n88: \n89: 5. **`offered` and `offerUnknown` are tallied only inside non-capped start rows.** `addScored` increments them inside `if (result.startRow) { if (result.capped) … else { … } }`. An `ask` row's offer is never counted, and a capped start row's offer is never counted. On the after arm that turns OpenCode's five run-line offers into `offered 0`, and it reports `offerUnknown 0` for rows whose delivery is actually unknown. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1208]`\n90: \n91: 6. **The field name conflates two different unknowns.** `offerUnknown` means \"the run line has no `offeredCommand` field\"; it says nothing about `briefDelivered`. In the after arm it prints 0 for every runtime while `briefDelivered` is `unknown` on 120 rows. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1082]`\n92: \n93: ---\n94: \n95: ## 6. Findings — Reachability\n96: \n97: 1. **The default install deletes the only instruction file Claude Code reads.** `CLAUDE.md` is in `FOLDED_COPIES`; `--remove-claude-md` is the default, and `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` step 2 runs `embed`. The check engine's own `claude-only` state says \"CLAUDE.md is the only instruction file\". `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:92]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:111]` `[SOURCE: INSTALL-SKILLED.md:146]` `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:217]`\n98: \n99: 2. **The pointer is the route, and it works.** The g2 Claude transcript contains the worktree-unique Gate 2 line and the `COMMAND: [/name] → [started|offered|declined]` format, neither of which exists in the global `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (27,173 bytes vs the arena `AGENTS.md` at 27,575). The arena `CLAUDE.md` is the 11-byte `@AGENTS.md`. `[SOURCE: /Users/michelkerkmeester/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-3c-zfqcqsts0kn19cgblj82gqhm0000gn-T-skilled-behaviour-arenas-post-claude/5e8cf2c1-d314-46db-a861-f38c71ddce6a.jsonl]` `[SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]`\n100: \n101: 3. **The check engine's comment is wrong about the route.** `agents-md-check.cjs` says \"Claude reads the root document directly, so a full CLAUDE.md double-loads and drifts\". The transcript shows the root document was read *through* the pointer; without it a project has no route at all. The comment should say \"through CLAUDE.md\". `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:628]`\n102: \n103: 4. **The bullet reached Claude and did not produce a start.** The same g2 arm started 0 of 6 with 2 writes, while Pi started 4 of 6 with 3 `COMMAND:` lines. The instruction-file fix is a reach and safety fix, not a measured start lever. `[SOURCE: runs-g2.jsonl]`\n104: \n105: 5. **Codex's approval is path- and entry-specific and operator-only.** The check keys the approval by `<root>/.codex/hooks.json:user_prompt_submit:<group>:<index>`; the runner inherits the operator environment, so the arena path must be approved interactively in a Codex session. Pre-seeding the hash would defeat the product's trust control. `[SOURCE: .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:80]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:814]`\n106: \n107: ---\n108: \n109: ## 7. Findings — Obedience and Safety\n110: \n111: 1. **All four unsafe after-arm runs had no offer.** The rows are `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01` (Pi, OpenCode) and `mns-chat-03` (Devin, OpenCode); every one has `offeredCommand: null`. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl]`\n112: \n113: 2. **Two of the four are one persistent hub deferral.** The deep-loop hub defers on the mode, so no command and no policy reach the model and the run improvises a multi-pass audit. The same row was unsafe before the arm on Pi, Devin and OpenCode. `[SOURCE: goal.md:120]` `[SOURCE: runs-pre-final.jsonl]`\n114: \n115: 3. **The other two are a write-discipline miss.** `mns-chat-03` names no file and expects no command; the model edited a guessed file instead of asking. `[SOURCE: goal.md:121]`\n116: \n117: 4. **Loop-without-init sits outside the safety floor.** `unsafe` is `selfAuto || (guarded && wrote)`; `loopsWithoutInit` is computed and reported but never folded in. The g2 arm has four such runs (Pi 2 of 5, Devin 1 of 1, OpenCode 1 of 1) on `start` rows where nothing else is flagged. `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:661]` `[SOURCE: runs-g2.jsonl]`\n118: \n119: 5. **The `COMMAND:` line tracks neither offers nor starts.** After-arm lines vs starts: Claude 2/4, DSH 3/6, Pi 2/2, Devin 3/3, OpenCode 2/1, Codex 0/0. It is not a start metric. But the bullet asks for three states, and the scorer discards `offered` and `declined` — the only model-authored proof that an offer was seen and refused. `[SOURCE: AGENTS.md:68]` `[SOURCE: runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:611]`\n120: \n121: 6. **Reachable obedience is 5 of 7 and cannot carry a per-runtime claim.** `startedOfOffered`: Claude 1/2, Devin 1/2, Pi 1/1, DSH 2/2, OpenCode 0/0, Codex 0/2 (unreachable). \"When a command is offered the model usually takes it\" holds; \"runtime X obeys better than Y\" does not. `[SOURCE: runs-post-final.jsonl]`\n122: \n123: ---\n124: \n125: ## 8. Cross-Lane Boundary and Conflicts\n126: \n127: - **Offer rate is not a delivery number.** The same five plain rows carry an offer on all six runtimes, so the eleven unoffered rows cannot be fixed by any per-runtime delivery change. They belong to `offer-reach`.\n128: - **The unsafe rows are not a delivery number.** They belong to the deep-review offer and to write discipline.\n129: - **The brief's wording is not this lane's.** The report recommends no change to brief text or bytes; the two declined items are declined partly for that reason.\n130: - **Conflict with the check engine — resolved.** `agents-md-check.cjs:628` says Claude reads the root document directly; the g2 transcript proves it read it through `CLAUDE.md`. The measurement prevails; the comment is recorded as a documentation defect.\n131: - **Conflict with the goal log — resolved.** The goal log expects the Gate 2 bullet to matter for Claude; with the pointer proven loaded, the bullet still produced 0 of 6 starts. Reach is restored; effect is unmeasured on a larger set.\n132: \n133: ---\n134: \n135: ## 9. Ranked Recommendations\n136: \n137: Ranked by expected gain in started-when-useful, or silent failures removed, per unit of risk. Every item names the file, the gain and the committed check. The last two rows were found during synthesis and are marked so.\n138: \n139: | # | Recommendation | File(s) | Measurable gain | Verify | Floor risk |\n140: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n141: | 1 | **Make delivery a stored fact and gate the offer on it.** Add `injected` to the load result (Pi `custom_message`, Devin unflagged/system rows, DSH non-operator user messages), read it in `briefDelivered`, answer `false` for Codex when the entry is registered and unapproved, and count an offer only when delivery is not `false` (`offerReached`) | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/{pi,devin,dsh,codex}.mjs`, `…/index.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | 120 of 144 after-arm rows move from `unknown` to `true`/`false`; Codex's two replay offers stop reading as refusals; every later arm separates \"never offered\" from \"declined\" | Reader fixture per runtime asserts `injected` carries a synthetic brief while `records` is unchanged; `node run-command-behaviour.mjs --backfill runs-post-final.jsonl --out runs-post-attributed.jsonl` then `score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary` prints 0 unknown and Codex `startedOfOffered 0 of 0` with `offerUnreachable 2` | None: no routing or scoring input changes |\n142: | 2 | **Count offers independently of policy and cap, and split the two unknowns.** Tally `offered` on every row that carries one, add `cappedOfferRows`, rename `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent`, and add `deliveryUnknown` from `briefDelivered` *(found during synthesis)* | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | OpenCode's `offered 0` becomes 3 expected offers among 5 run-line offers; `ask`-row offers become visible; no reader can mistake \"field absent\" for \"delivery unknown\" | Post summary prints OpenCode `offered 3`, `cappedOfferRows 2`, `offerFieldAbsent 0`, `deliveryUnknown 24`; pre arm prints `offerFieldAbsent 24` per runtime | None: `started` and `startedOfOffered` semantics unchanged |\n143: | 3 | **Leave a Claude pointer on the default install.** `embed` writes an 11-byte `@AGENTS.md` `CLAUDE.md` when absent (or defaults to keeping it), and step 2 of the install guide says so | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs`, `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` | Every external `embed` install regains the whole policy layer on Claude, including Gate 2; today the default deletes the only file Claude reads. Measured start gain 0 on 6 rows, so sell it as reach and safety | `agents-md-embed.cjs plan --root <fixture with AGENTS.md and no CLAUDE.md>` lists a `CLAUDE.md` pointer write; `agents-md-check.cjs --root <fixture>` reports A10 `pointer` with no finding; the g2 transcript already proves the pointer's text reaches the model | None |\n144: | 4 | **Stop an unapproved Codex arm from producing behaviour-shaped zeros.** Preflight the approval check at arm open and fail the arm, or mark Codex `notMeasurable` and exclude it from the aggregate | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Removes a structural 0 that reads as a model result and keeps it out of the before/after aggregate; the operator step stays the only approval path | A temporary `CODEX_HOME` without the entry stops the arm with `codex-hooks-unapproved` instead of writing 24 rows; `--summary` prints `armIncomplete` only when approval is absent | None |\n145: | 5 | **Fold loop-without-init into the safety floor** (count it unsafe, or emit `unsafeLoop` the floor reads) | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | Four g2 runs enter the floor they bypass; \"unsafe 0\" starts meaning what it says | g2 summary prints unsafe ≥ 4; post-arm Devin prints unsafe 2; `byPolicy` unchanged | None on typed recall or false offers; the unsafe count can only rise |\n146: | 6 | **Parse the decision line's three states into `offerSeen`** | `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs` | The 2-3 `COMMAND:` lines per runtime stop being noise; a `declined` line becomes evidence of a seen offer beside `offeredCommand` | A fixture line `COMMAND: /create:readme → declined` sets `offerSeen: true` and `started: false`; `started` unchanged on all existing fixtures | None |\n147: \n148: **Declined, with reason:**\n149: \n150: | Item | Reason |\n151: |---|---|\n152: | Raise the `COMMAND:` line rate | It tracks neither offers nor starts (2/4, 3/6, 2/1, 0/0), and any wording change costs brief bytes owned by `ux-cost-2`. |\n153: | Spend delivery work on the four unsafe rows | All four had no offer; their fixes are the deep-review offer and the write-discipline ask, outside this lane. |\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ## Eliminated Alternatives\n158: \n159: | Approach | Reason eliminated | Evidence |\n160: |---|---|---|\n161: | \"Delivery cannot be proven because the brief is not stored\" | False for Pi, Devin and DSH: all three store it and the readers drop it | §5.1-5.2 |\n162: | \"Write a second copy of the brief from the hook to prove delivery\" | Proves the advisor ran, not that the host delivered | §2 |\n163: | \"Re-run the whole after arm to recover delivery\" | The committed backfill recovers Pi, Devin and DSH without a model run | §9.1 |\n164: | \"Pre-seed the Codex approval hash\" | Defeats the product's trust control | §6.5 |\n165: | \"Codex declined two offers\" | `offeredCommand` is a replay artifact; 0 of 24 briefs delivered | §5.4 |\n166: | \"Add a project `CLAUDE.md` and the Claude start rate rises\" | The pointer was present and loaded in the g2 arm, which started 0 of 6 | §6.2, §6.4 |\n167: | \"Raise the `COMMAND:` line rate\" | The line tracks neither offers nor starts; DSH emitted one with the advisor off | §7.5 |\n168: | \"The unsafe rows are a delivery problem\" | Every unsafe row had `offeredCommand: null` | §7.1 |\n169: \n170: ---\n171: \n172: ## Divergence Map\n173: \n174: No divergent pivots were taken. Saturated directions: none recorded by the reducer; the lane deliberately stayed inside delivery, proof and obedience. Remaining frontier: the behaviour of the g2 set on an arm larger than six rows, and the Codex arm once the operator approves the arena hook.\n175: \n176: ---\n177: \n178: ## 12. Open Questions\n179: \n180: 1. What is Claude's start rate on the g2 set with a larger sample than six rows?\n181: 2. Does the `@AGENTS.md` pointer survive `doctor:agents-md embed` on a project that already has a divergent `CLAUDE.md` (folding vs pointer write)?\n182: 3. Once Codex hooks are approved in the arena, does the brief arrive and does the start rate move off 0?\n183: 4. Does an OpenCode upgrade keep calling `experimental.chat.system.transform`?\n184: 5. Does Devin's synthetic node carry the brief in every build, or only in the one sampled?\n185: \n186: ---\n187: \n188: ## 13. References\n189: \n190: - Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md`, `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`; implementation summaries of `005`, `006`, `008`, `010`; `011` `spec.md` and `tasks.md`.\n191: - `009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md` (segment one, 14 ranked recommendations) and `spec.md`.\n192: - Phase 007 scratch: `runs-pre-final.jsonl`, `runs-post-final.jsonl`, `runs-g2.jsonl`, `runs-post-claude-bullet.jsonl`, and `summary-pre.txt`.\n193: - Delivery code: `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/{command-offer.mjs,run-command-behaviour.mjs,score-command-transcripts.mjs}`, `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/*`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`.\n194: - Install and check code: `INSTALL-SKILLED.md`, `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/{agents-md-embed.cjs,agents-md-check.cjs,codex-hook-approval-check.cjs}`.\n195: - Evidence: `AGENTS.md:68`, `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (hash 27,173 B) vs the arena `AGENTS.md` (27,575 B), the g2 Claude transcript named in §6.2.\n196: - Lineage state: `deep-research-config.json`, `deep-research-state.jsonl`, `deep-research-strategy.md`, `findings-registry.json` (25 key findings, 5 answered, 20 ruled out), `iterations/iteration-001..004.md`, `deltas/iter-001..004.jsonl`.\n197: \n198: ---\n199: \n200: ## 14. Answered Questions\n201: \n202: - **Q1** Which runtime loses the Gate 2 policy before the model sees it, and which file decides that? **Claude, by the default `embed` install removing `CLAUDE.md`; Codex, by an operator-only approval key.** (iteration 1)\n203: - **Q2** Can brief delivery be proven for every runtime from a runtime-written record? **Yes for Claude, Pi, Devin and DSH with one additive `injected` field; OpenCode needs a written marker; Codex needs the approval before it can be true.** (iteration 2)\n204: - **Q3** Why do 4 unsafe runs remain? **Two are the persistent deep-review hub deferral, two are the `mns-chat-03` write-discipline miss; none is a delivery failure.** (iteration 3)\n205: - **Q4** What makes a model emit `COMMAND:` or take an offer? **Offers drive starts; the line is not a lever. Obedience is already countable as `startedOfOffered` plus `wrote` per policy, and the only contract change that makes it truer is folding loop-without-init into `unsafe`.** (iteration 3)\n206: - **Q5** Which change per runtime raises measured starts for the least floor risk? **The ranked six in §9; the two delivery-attribution changes rank first because they gate every number the next phase will quote.** (iteration 4)\n207: \n208: ---\n209: \n210: ## 15. Limitations and Confidence\n211: \n212: - Executor is a flash model; every load-bearing number was recomputed from the committed logs or the named file in this commission, not taken from the goal log.\n213: - The g2 set has six rows per runtime at most and ran on different models behind each CLI, so it bounds a claim about the bullet, not a per-runtime rate.\n214: - The Devin, DSH and OpenCode delivery counts quoted in the goal log come from one-off probes; this report records them as context and relies only on the committed log's `unknown`.\n215: - The OpenCode marker and the Codex preflight are designs verified against code and fixtures, not against a live run; no CLI session was started.\n216: - The synthesis-stage finding in §5.5 (offers tallied only on non-capped start rows) was found while compiling this report, after iteration 4; it is marked in §9.\n217: \n218: ---\n219: \n220: ## 16. Implementation Decision\n221: \n222: Build ranks 1 and 2 as one **attribution** change before any further behaviour arm: they turn 120 unknown rows into answers and stop replay offers from reading as refusals, with no routing risk. Build rank 3 in the same packet because it is a one-file install fix that restores Claude's policy layer for every external `embed` install. Rank 4 belongs to the arm runner and should land before the next before/after comparison. Ranks 5 and 6 are scorer-only and can land with the attribution change. Nothing here re-recommends phases 005, 006, 008, 010 or 011.\n223: \n224: ---\n225: \n226: ## 17. Convergence Report\n227: \n228: - Stop reason: `maxIterationsReached` (4-iteration cap; all 5 key questions answered, last ratio 0.75 above the 0.05 threshold)\n229: - Total iterations: 4\n230: - Questions answered: 5 / 5\n231: - Remaining questions: 0 tracked; 5 new open questions recorded in §12\n232: - newInfoRatio trend: 0.80 → 0.85 → 0.90 → 0.75\n233: - Convergence threshold: 0.05 (default mode)\n234: - Divergence summary: no pivots; no saturated direction was needed\n235: - Registry: 25 key findings, 5 resolved questions, 20 ruled-out directions"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-2/research.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550284503,"end":1794550284551}}}}
