{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550326911,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d388e43a001xiwR6LBX0HHyca","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d388bedf001ry46olpWnNpA3R","type":"tool","id":"call_00_23dmmi79dydymlj1yud0kb4e","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-3 delivery truth and command visibility\ndescription: Segment-three cross-CLI lane: OpenCode plugin brief beside the hook brief, Claude's 32-of-44 command visibility, and whether phase 013's attribution reads true per runtime.\n---\n\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-3\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nEstablish, per runtime, what each CLI actually renders into the model's context after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built: where the OpenCode plugin brief still differs from the hook brief for the same prompt, which commands each runtime's own command surface exposes to its operator, and whether the committed attribution now reports delivery truthfully on all six runtimes.\n\n### Usage\n\n- Reads the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), the built state of phases 011, 012 and 013 and their scratch evidence, then the code at HEAD.\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\n\n### Question Injection Surface\n\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\nSEGMENT THREE, cross-CLI lane: after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built and committed, what still limits command surfacing across runtimes — the OpenCode plugin brief beside the hook brief, the Claude Code 32-of-44 command visibility collapse, and whether phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] (d) After the plugin mapper fix, what still differs between the OpenCode plugin brief and the hook brief for the same prompt — wording, fields, order, bytes, command line, policy, fail-open path — rendered side by side from code or a renderer run?\n- [ ] (e) Claude Code lists 32 of 44 commands because a command file named `skill.md` collapses its folder: which options keep every operator-facing command name intact, what does each cost per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), and what check proves 44 of 44?\n- [ ] Does phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime on the committed after arm, and where does it still overstate or understate reach?\n- [ ] Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by started-when-useful gain per unit of floor risk, and what file does each fix change?\n- [ ] What does the degraded (daemon-unreachable) path lose per runtime that the live path keeps, and what is the smallest change that makes the fallback carry the same command?\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- Re-recommending anything ranked, built, declined or eliminated in segment one (`research/research.md`, `spec.md` dispositions) or segment two (`research/research-segment-2.md` sections 3 and 4). Reopen only with a new measurement that changes a disposition, naming the rank and the measurement.\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\n- Offer-rate tuning for plain rows (lane `offer-reach-3`, questions a and b).\n- Hook-health default and brief byte cost (lane `ux-cost-3`, questions c and f), except where a render difference changes bytes measurably.\n- Starting CLI, arena or daemon sessions; starting ollama; editing anything outside this lineage.\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from `command-prompts.jsonl`, or reading `holdout-prompts.jsonl` at all.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Max 6 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n- Completed pivots: 0\n- Failed pivots: 0\n- Audited overrides: 0\n- Saturated: none yet\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n[None yet]\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n(d) Render the OpenCode plugin brief and the hook brief for the same prompt from the two code paths, then diff them field by field.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\n\n- Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md` log (after-arm numbers, phase 011/012/013 rows), `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`.\n- Built state: `011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md`, `012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md`, `013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md`.\n- Scratch evidence: `011/scratch/{after.txt,suite-after.txt,brief-cost.json,hook-health.json,typed-heads.json}`, `012/scratch/{after-final.txt,after-final-policy.txt,live-heads.txt,chat-after.json,routes-*.tsv}`, `013/scratch/{after.txt,delivery-leg.txt,runs-post-attributed.jsonl,summary-*-after.json}`.\n- Renderer and plugin: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/`.\n- Visibility: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/`, `.claude/commands/`.\n- Attribution: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/{command-offer.mjs,score-command-transcripts.mjs,run-command-behaviour.mjs}`.\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Source pointers: hook renderer, OpenCode plugin mapper, per-runtime command mirror trees, session readers and the scorer.\n- Reuse candidates: the committed plugin probe, the capture and floor scripts, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`.\n- Integration points: hook registration per runtime, mirror sync, brief rendering, delivery probe.\n- Constraints: read-only git, no CLI sessions, no ollama, no writes outside the lineage.\n\n---\n\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n- Max iterations: 6\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\n- Progressive synthesis: true\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\n- Current generation: 1\n- Started: 2026-11-13T07:40:00.000Z\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deep-research-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deep-research-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-3 delivery truth and command visibility\\ndescription: Segment-three cross-CLI lane: OpenCode plugin brief beside the hook brief, Claude's 32-of-44 command visibility, and whether phase 013's attribution reads true per runtime.\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Research Strategy - cross-cli-3\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nEstablish, per runtime, what each CLI actually renders into the model's context after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built: where the OpenCode plugin brief still differs from the hook brief for the same prompt, which commands each runtime's own command surface exposes to its operator, and whether the committed attribution now reports delivery truthfully on all six runtimes.\\n\\n### Usage\\n\\n- Reads the parent packet (`008-command-surfacing-build`), the built state of phases 011, 012 and 013 and their scratch evidence, then the code at HEAD.\\n- Writes only inside this lineage directory.\\n- Reducer owns Sections 3, 6, 7-11A.\\n\\n### Question Injection Surface\\n\\n`inbox.jsonl` in this lineage directory if an external question appears.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\nSEGMENT THREE, cross-CLI lane: after phases 011, 012 and 013 are built and committed, what still limits command surfacing across runtimes — the OpenCode plugin brief beside the hook brief, the Claude Code 32-of-44 command visibility collapse, and whether phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] (d) After the plugin mapper fix, what still differs between the OpenCode plugin brief and the hook brief for the same prompt — wording, fields, order, bytes, command line, policy, fail-open path — rendered side by side from code or a renderer run?\\n- [ ] (e) Claude Code lists 32 of 44 commands because a command file named `skill.md` collapses its folder: which options keep every operator-facing command name intact, what does each cost per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), and what check proves 44 of 44?\\n- [ ] Does phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime on the committed after arm, and where does it still overstate or understate reach?\\n- [ ] Which remaining cross-CLI gap ranks first by started-when-useful gain per unit of floor risk, and what file does each fix change?\\n- [ ] What does the degraded (daemon-unreachable) path lose per runtime that the live path keeps, and what is the smallest change that makes the fallback carry the same command?\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- Re-recommending anything ranked, built, declined or eliminated in segment one (`research/research.md`, `spec.md` dispositions) or segment two (`research/research-segment-2.md` sections 3 and 4). Reopen only with a new measurement that changes a disposition, naming the rank and the measurement.\\n- Implementing any fix (research only).\\n- Offer-rate tuning for plain rows (lane `offer-reach-3`, questions a and b).\\n- Hook-health default and brief byte cost (lane `ux-cost-3`, questions c and f), except where a render difference changes bytes measurably.\\n- Starting CLI, arena or daemon sessions; starting ollama; editing anything outside this lineage.\\n- Reading or printing holdout prompt text from `command-prompts.jsonl`, or reading `holdout-prompts.jsonl` at all.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Max 6 iterations, convergence threshold 0.05 after the 3-iteration floor.\\n- Stop early only at legal convergence; record the reason in research.md.\\n- No writes outside this lineage directory; spec.md writeback and continuity save are deferred and recorded as scope decisions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n## 7. WHAT WORKED\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n## 8. WHAT FAILED\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\\n- Completed pivots: 0\\n- Failed pivots: 0\\n- Audited overrides: 0\\n- Saturated: none yet\\n- Pivot lineage: none yet\\n- Remaining frontier: none recorded\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\\n[None yet]\\n\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\\n(d) Render the OpenCode plugin brief and the hook brief for the same prompt from the two code paths, then diff them field by field.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\\n## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\nEvidence pointers (read-only):\\n\\n- Parent packet `008-command-surfacing-build`: `goal.md` log (after-arm numbers, phase 011/012/013 rows), `spec.md`, `decision-record.md`.\\n- Built state: `011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md`, `012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md`, `013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md`.\\n- Scratch evidence: `011/scratch/{after.txt,suite-after.txt,brief-cost.json,hook-health.json,typed-heads.json}`, `012/scratch/{after-final.txt,after-final-policy.txt,live-heads.txt,chat-after.json,routes-*.tsv}`, `013/scratch/{after.txt,delivery-leg.txt,runs-post-attributed.jsonl,summary-*-after.json}`.\\n- Renderer and plugin: `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts`, `.opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js`, `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/`.\\n- Visibility: `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `.skilled/commands/`, `.claude/commands/`.\\n- Attribution: `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/`, `runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/{command-offer.mjs,score-command-transcripts.mjs,run-command-behaviour.mjs}`.\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Source pointers: hook renderer, OpenCode plugin mapper, per-runtime command mirror trees, session readers and the scorer.\\n- Reuse candidates: the committed plugin probe, the capture and floor scripts, `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`.\\n- Integration points: hook registration per runtime, mirror sync, brief rendering, delivery probe.\\n- Constraints: read-only git, no CLI sessions, no ollama, no writes outside the lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\\n- Max iterations: 6\\n- Convergence threshold: 0.05\\n- Per-iteration budget: 24 tool calls, 10 minutes\\n- Progressive synthesis: true\\n- research.md ownership: workflow-owned canonical synthesis output\\n- Lifecycle branches: `resume`, `restart` (live); `fork`, `completed-continue` (deferred)\\n- Machine-owned sections: reducer controls Sections 3, 6, 7-11A\\n- Canonical pause sentinel: `.deep-research-pause`\\n- Current generation: 1\\n- Started: 2026-11-13T07:40:00.000Z\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deep-research-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550326330,"end":1794550326911}}}}
