{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550596748,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38d039c001cXs86a6Z8Q145X","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d38cdda5001t25XcMj4xJcaQ3","type":"tool","id":"call_00_79wx69zi4fguxa2vxbau42f5","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"COLLAPSE|32/44|32 of 44|collapse\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --glob '!**/lineages/**' | head -30"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:51:- A visibility count and a collapse guard in `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, hook health in `advisor_status` and the `/doctor:setup` advisor leg, a prove-it install step, a head length test and `measure-brief-cost.mjs`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:126:The deriver printed `stale` because a worker was mid-edit, so its fresh state is recorded again by T001. The last command counts the Claude command mirrors per folder, `true` meaning the folder holds `skill.md`. The folder with an empty name is the private, untracked `local-skilled-alignment.md`, so the 44 tracked commands show as 32 on Claude Code: 31 outside `create/` plus the one entry the collapsed folder becomes. No holdout row was opened. Every probed row has split `none`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:143:- Rank 9: `create/skill.md` collapses its folder on Claude Code. Confirmed by `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt` (listing A shows one `create` entry and no `create:readme`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:144:- Rank 9: `--check` prints `claude 32/44` today. Refuted: `checkMirrors` prints only a PASS line or drift lines (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:316-346`). The number itself is right: the count above gives 32 of 44.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:145:- Rank 9: `--check` is where a guard blocks a new collapse. Confirmed: the pre-commit hook runs it (`.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:437`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:161:- Guards: the visibility count and collapse guard (rank 9, second half), hook health in status, the setup leg and the install guide (rank 12), the head length test and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` (rank 14, two items).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:188:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, its test and its README | Modify | Visibility line and collapse guard |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:219:| REQ-008 | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` prints `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` on this tree, and exits 1 with a `COLLAPSE` line when any command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:313:- Does a new file inside `create/` fail the guard? Decision: no, only a new `skill.md` in another folder fails (Recommended). That is the act that collapses a folder, and the existing case stays on a one-entry allowlist.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/spec.md:197:  - Claude Code sees 32 of 44 tracked commands. The mirror check prints `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` (`../011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:147:| A hub does not repeat a command whose own row ranks in the same result | An alignment finding: the earlier collapse check grouped bridge rows only and missed a hub attaching the same command |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:9:  - \"same owner collapse\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:66:- A same-owner collapse so a command row and its owner skill never form an ambiguous pair.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:154:| `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Modify | Regenerated bridge blocks, and the same-owner collapse in the Python ranking |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:155:| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts` | Modify | Same-owner collapse before top-K and the same-owner exclusion from the ambiguity cluster |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:198:| REQ-013 | Rows that resolve to one command collapse to one entry before the top-K cut, in both scorers, so a prompt never spends two of three slots on one command. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:29:The deriver emits a `TRACKED_COMMANDS` table that gives every tracked runnable its policy, its owner skill and whether the TypeScript scorer has a row for it. Two helpers read it: one finds the typed command in a prompt and one says whether the top recommendation may carry it. The recommend handler uses them to attach a typed command to its owner on top, the scorer uses them to put the owner first when the command has no row of its own and the capture uses them to report the typed block. The guards are independent: a count and a collapse check in the mirror script, hook health in the status output, a head length test and a cost script.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:65:- **Guards**: `commandVisibility` and a `COLLAPSE` drift line in `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `hookHealth` in `advisor_status`, a line under the setup leg, an install step, `command-head-length.vitest.ts` and `measure-brief-cost.mjs`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:88:| `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` | Link drift only | Visibility line and collapse guard | T004 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:30:    - merge/migration/consolidation narratives (consolidate*, merged from, renamed from, collapsed, X→Y, reorganization history)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/graph-metadata.json:18:      \"same owner collapse\",\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/graph-metadata.json:39:      \"collapse\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/scratch/launch/topic3.txt:1:SEGMENT THREE. Phases 011, 012 and 013 are BUILT and committed. Find what still limits command surfacing after them, from the built state and measurements, not from the plans. P = specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build. READ FIRST: P/goal.md; the built state of the three new phases, which is P/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md, P/012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md and P/013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md, plus the after files in their scratch folders (P/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/scratch/after.txt, suite-after.txt, brief-cost.json and hook-health.json; every file named after*, *-after.* or *after*.tsv under P/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch and P/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch); then the code at HEAD those summaries name. ALREADY DECIDED, DO NOT RE-RECOMMEND: everything ranked, built, declined or eliminated in segment one (P/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research.md and its dispositions in P/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/spec.md) and in segment two (P/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/research-segment-2.md, sections 3 and 4). Reopen one only with a new measurement that changes its disposition, and name the rank and the measurement. CARRIED QUESTIONS, each answered with evidence (the command you ran and its output, or file:line): (a) which plain tune rows of .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-prompts.jsonl still get no command after phase 012, and why, by row id. Use `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs` (without --write), `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"<tune prompt>\"}' --format json` per row, and `node .skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <hub> --prompt \"<tune prompt>\"` where a hub defers. Name the cause per row: no command evidence, hub defers, below threshold, policy or cap, wrong top. (b) intent-signal enrichment and re-embedding of the skill graph, declined in segment two at rank 15: which tune rows it would move, measured where you can without writing outside your lineage folder (a real-embedding capture with --real-embedding only against an Ollama server that is already running), its risk to the floors, and the cost of keeping the vectors in step with the metadata. (c) hook health shows in /doctor:setup only after a run with SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1: what should the default be, and at what cost in bytes written per prompt, latency per prompt, file growth and privacy of what is recorded; read the diagnostics writer and the advisor_status reader. (d) OpenCode: after the plugin mapper fix, what else differs between the plugin brief and the hook brief for the same prompt (wording, fields, order, bytes, command line, policy, fail-open path); show the two renders side by side from code or from a run of the renderer, not from memory. (e) Claude Code lists 32 of 44 commands because a command file named skill.md collapses its folder: list every option that does not rename an operator-facing command (for example a runtime mirror or alias file, a generated pointer, a namespace change in the mirror only), with its cost per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh) and how a check would prove 44 of 44. (f) cold start and token cost of the brief per prompt, measured: `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-brief-cost.mjs` (it uses its own temporary socket and refuses holdout rows) and `node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/measure-embedder-cost.mjs` (only against an Ollama server that is already running), and any cut to the brief that loses no information, proven by showing the same command, policy and skill reach the model before and after. YOUR LANE is named by your lineage label: `offer-reach-3` = (a) and (b), `cross-cli-3` = (d) and (e) plus whether phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime, `ux-cost-3` = (c) and (f). Read another lane's question only when it blocks yours. RULES: every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain (which rows, bytes, milliseconds or runtimes move, and by how much), and how to verify it with a committed script or test, plus its risk to the floors as P/012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md states them (segment two used typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and scorer [159,50,20,5]). Rank by expected gain in started-when-useful per unit of risk. A claim with no command output or file:line behind it is labelled inference. NEVER read or print the prompt text of a row whose split is holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, and never read holdout-prompts.jsonl: use counts only. Tune and none rows may be read. Do not start any model CLI session, arena or daemon, never start ollama (a server that does not answer is a recorded gap, not a reason to start one), and do not edit or write any file outside your lineage folder; a scratch copy, if you need one, lives inside it. Repository root for all reads and writes: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/tasks.md:53:- [ ] T013 Answer or carry forward in segment three the questions segment two left open (`research/`). Verify: each is marked answered or carried forward with a reason. The questions are: plain reach on the holdout split is 1 of 44 while the tune split reads 23 of 45, so the phase 012 gains do not transfer to unseen wording. Hook health shows in `/doctor:setup` only after a run with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`. The fallback scorer loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers when the daemon is unreachable (`../012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt`). Claude Code sees 32 of 44 tracked commands. Questions 3 and 4 of `research/research.md` section 12 and rank 15 of segment two.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:29:Seven workstreams: harness, attach, phrases, one activation source, read-only from the class and same-owner collapse run in order, and doctor phrases run beside attach through read-only. The attach rule is one exported pure function that the handler and the harness both call, so the harness measures the shipped rule and can be proven neutral before any scorer change. The proof is the extended phase 1 capture reporting own-row and attached reach per split, false offers at 0 of 35, the four pinned numbers no worse and no typed command ambiguous with its own owner.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:57:Attach, project, collapse. A hub command rides on its owner skill, a non-hub command is projected from metadata into its own row, and rows for one command collapse to one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:69:- **Same-owner collapse**: rows whose bridge resolves to one command merge before the top-K cut in `fusion.ts` and in the Python ranking, and `clustersWithTop` (`ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts:32-48`) never clusters a command row with its own owner skill.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:72:The scorer ranks skills and the now active non-hub command rows, collapses rows for one command, cuts to top K and sets `ambiguous` from `isAmbiguousTopTwo` (`fusion.ts:1403`). The handler asks `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt-stdin` for each eligible hub, through `compiledRouteForRecommendation` (`advisor-recommend.ts:364`), and passes the result with the skill id and prompt to `attachCommand`. When the route is `action: route`, `selectionKind: single`, with one target whose mode is in `MODE_COMMANDS`, the command lands on that recommendation as `command`. For `system-deep-loop` the function also requires depth wording, per decision D3. The hook asks for the route of its top passing hub only and keeps the field. The harness runs the same scorer, asks the same front door for the top hub's route and calls the same function. Doctor rows reach their command as own rows, through bridge ids the harness already maps to commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:115:Setup rebuilds `ADV`, reproduces the phase 1 baseline and the four pinned numbers, saves both and times the hook. Implementation runs the seven workstreams, starting with the neutral harness extension in `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, authoring doctor phrases in `_routes.yaml` beside attach through read-only and ending with the same-owner collapse in `fusion.ts`, `ambiguity.ts` and `skill_advisor.py`. Verification rebuilds, re-captures, compares reach, false offers, the pinned numbers and ambiguity with the baseline, times the hook again and runs the whole suite.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:184:W1 harness (neutral) ──► W2 attach ──► W3 phrases ──► W4 activation ──► W5 read-only ──► W6 collapse ──► verify\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:51:- A visibility count and a collapse guard in `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check`, hook health in `advisor_status` and the `/doctor:setup` advisor leg, a prove-it install step, a head length test and `measure-brief-cost.mjs`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:126:The deriver printed `stale` because a worker was mid-edit, so its fresh state is recorded again by T001. The last command counts the Claude command mirrors per folder, `true` meaning the folder holds `skill.md`. The folder with an empty name is the private, untracked `local-skilled-alignment.md`, so the 44 tracked commands show as 32 on Claude Code: 31 outside `create/` plus the one entry the collapsed folder becomes. No holdout row was opened. Every probed row has split `none`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:143:- Rank 9: `create/skill.md` collapses its folder on Claude Code. Confirmed by `../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt` (listing A shows one `create` entry and no `create:readme`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:144:- Rank 9: `--check` prints `claude 32/44` today. Refuted: `checkMirrors` prints only a PASS line or drift lines (`.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:316-346`). The number itself is right: the count above gives 32 of 44.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:145:- Rank 9: `--check` is where a guard blocks a new collapse. Confirmed: the pre-commit hook runs it (`.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:437`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:161:- Guards: the visibility count and collapse guard (rank 9, second half), hook health in status, the setup leg and the install guide (rank 12), the head length test and `measure-brief-cost.mjs` (rank 14, two items).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:188:| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, its test and its README | Modify | Visibility line and collapse guard |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:219:| REQ-008 | `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` prints `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` on this tree, and exits 1 with a `COLLAPSE` line when any command folder other than `create/` holds a `skill.md`. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/spec.md:313:- Does a new file inside `create/` fail the guard? Decision: no, only a new `skill.md` in another folder fails (Recommended). That is the act that collapses a folder, and the existing case stays on a one-entry allowlist.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/spec.md:197:  - Claude Code sees 32 of 44 tracked commands. The mirror check prints `visibility claude 32/44, cursor 44/44` (`../011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/implementation-summary.md`).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/implementation-summary.md:147:| A hub does not repeat a command whose own row ranks in the same result | An alignment finding: the earlier collapse check grouped bridge rows only and missed a hub attaching the same command |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:9:  - \"same owner collapse\"\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:66:- A same-owner collapse so a command row and its owner skill never form an ambiguous pair.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:154:| `ADV/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `ADV/scripts/skill_advisor.py` | Modify | Regenerated bridge blocks, and the same-owner collapse in the Python ranking |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:155:| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts` | Modify | Same-owner collapse before top-K and the same-owner exclusion from the ambiguity cluster |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/spec.md:198:| REQ-013 | Rows that resolve to one command collapse to one entry before the top-K cut, in both scorers, so a prompt never spends two of three slots on one command. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:29:The deriver emits a `TRACKED_COMMANDS` table that gives every tracked runnable its policy, its owner skill and whether the TypeScript scorer has a row for it. Two helpers read it: one finds the typed command in a prompt and one says whether the top recommendation may carry it. The recommend handler uses them to attach a typed command to its owner on top, the scorer uses them to put the owner first when the command has no row of its own and the capture uses them to report the typed block. The guards are independent: a count and a collapse check in the mirror script, hook health in the status output, a head length test and a cost script.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:65:- **Guards**: `commandVisibility` and a `COLLAPSE` drift line in `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs`, `hookHealth` in `advisor_status`, a line under the setup leg, an install step, `command-head-length.vitest.ts` and `measure-brief-cost.mjs`.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/011-typed-command-delivery-and-guards/plan.md:88:| `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` | Link drift only | Visibility line and collapse guard | T004 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:30:    - merge/migration/consolidation narratives (consolidate*, merged from, renamed from, collapsed, X→Y, reorganization history)\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/graph-metadata.json:18:      \"same owner collapse\",\nspecs