o the brief that loses no information, proven by showing the same command, policy and skill reach the model before and after. YOUR LANE is named by your lineage label: `offer-reach-3` = (a) and (b), `cross-cli-3` = (d) and (e) plus whether phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime, `ux-cost-3` = (c) and (f). Read another lane's question only when it blocks yours. RULES: every recommendation names the file it changes, the measurable gain (which rows, bytes, milliseconds or runtimes move, and by how much), and how to verify it with a committed script or test, plus its risk to the floors as P/012-plain-offer-reach/implementation-summary.md states them (segment two used typed recall 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35 and scorer [159,50,20,5]). Rank by expected gain in started-when-useful per unit of risk. A claim with no command output or file:line behind it is labelled inference. NEVER read or print the prompt text of a row whose split is holdout in command-prompts.jsonl, and never read holdout-prompts.jsonl: use counts only. Tune and none rows may be read. Do not start any model CLI session, arena or daemon, never start ollama (a server that does not answer is a recorded gap, not a reason to start one), and do not edit or write any file outside your lineage folder; a scratch copy, if you need one, lives inside it. Repository root for all reads and writes: /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/tasks.md:53:- [ ] T013 Answer or carry forward in segment three the questions segment two left open (`research/`). Verify: each is marked answered or carried forward with a reason. The questions are: plain reach on the holdout split is 1 of 44 while the tune split reads 23 of 45, so the phase 012 gains do not transfer to unseen wording. Hook health shows in `/doctor:setup` only after a run with `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG=1`. The fallback scorer loses the mode label, the doctor hand-off and plain offers when the daemon is unreachable (`../012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt`). Claude Code sees 32 of 44 tracked commands. Questions 3 and 4 of `research/research.md` section 12 and rank 15 of segment two.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:29:Seven workstreams: harness, attach, phrases, one activation source, read-only from the class and same-owner collapse run in order, and doctor phrases run beside attach through read-only. The attach rule is one exported pure function that the handler and the harness both call, so the harness measures the shipped rule and can be proven neutral before any scorer change. The proof is the extended phase 1 capture reporting own-row and attached reach per split, false offers at 0 of 35, the four pinned numbers no worse and no typed command ambiguous with its own owner.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:57:Attach, project, collapse. A hub command rides on its owner skill, a non-hub command is projected from metadata into its own row, and rows for one command collapse to one.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:69:- **Same-owner collapse**: rows whose bridge resolves to one command merge before the top-K cut in `fusion.ts` and in the Python ranking, and `clustersWithTop` (`ADV/lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts:32-48`) never clusters a command row with its own owner skill.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:72:The scorer ranks skills and the now active non-hub command rows, collapses rows for one command, cuts to top K and sets `ambiguous` from `isAmbiguousTopTwo` (`fusion.ts:1403`). The handler asks `.skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs --hub <id> --prompt-stdin` for each eligible hub, through `compiledRouteForRecommendation` (`advisor-recommend.ts:364`), and passes the result with the skill id and prompt to `attachCommand`. When the route is `action: route`, `selectionKind: single`, with one target whose mode is in `MODE_COMMANDS`, the command lands on that recommendation as `command`. For `system-deep-loop` the function also requires depth wording, per decision D3. The hook asks for the route of its top passing hub only and keeps the field. The harness runs the same scorer, asks the same front door for the top hub's route and calls the same function. Doctor rows reach their command as own rows, through bridge ids the harness already maps to commands.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:115:Setup rebuilds `ADV`, reproduces the phase 1 baseline and the four pinned numbers, saves both and times the hook. Implementation runs the seven workstreams, starting with the neutral harness extension in `capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs`, authoring doctor phrases in `_routes.yaml` beside attach through read-only and ending with the same-owner collapse in `fusion.ts`, `ambiguity.ts` and `skill_advisor.py`. Verification rebuilds, re-captures, compares reach, false offers, the pinned numbers and ambiguity with the baseline, times the hook again and runs the whole suite.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/003-plain-chat-command-reach/plan.md:184:W1 harness (neutral) ──► W2 attach ──► W3 phrases ──► W4 activation ──► W5 read-only ──► W6 collapse ──► verify\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \\\"COLLAPSE|32/44|32 of 44|collapse\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build --glob '!**/lineages/**' | head -30\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550596508,"end":1794550596748}}}}
