way folders outside any repository.\nlisting-a.txt: create/readme.md and create/skill.md present. The Skill tool lists one entry, `create`. `create:readme` is absent.\nlisting-b.txt: create/readme.md and create/new-skill.md present. The Skill tool lists `create:new-skill` and `create:readme`.\nCause: a command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill named after the folder, which hides every sibling command in that folder.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ndescription: Create or update OpenCode skills via one unified command with operation routing. :auto/:confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<skill-name> [operation] [type] [--path <dir>] [--chained] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:skill Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\nRoute /create:skill to its presentation contract and workflow YAML for creating or updating OpenCode skills through the unified skill command.\n\n- Do not split behavior across legacy command definitions.\n- Do not edit workflow YAML while executing this command.\n\n---\n\n## 2. OWNED ASSETS\n=== readme cmd\n---\ndescription: Folder README creation, general or code-folder, with sk-doc quality standards. Modes :auto, :confirm.\nargument-hint: \"<target> [--type <project|component|feature|skill>] [--output <path>] [:auto|:confirm]\"\nallowed-tools: Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, TodoWrite\n---\n\n# /create:readme Router\n\nThis command is a thin router. It separates execution routing from user-facing presentation.\n\n## 1. ROUTER CONTRACT\n\n=== g5\nG5 cause confirmed on 2026-11-12, Claude Code with claude-sonnet-5-5, two throwaway folders outside any repository.\nlisting-a.txt: create/readme.md and create/skill.md present. The Skill tool lists one entry, `create`. `create:readme` is absent.\nlisting-b.txt: create/readme.md and create/new-skill.md present. The Skill tool lists `create:new-skill` and `create:readme`.\nCause: a command file named skill.md makes Claude Code read its folder as one skill named after the folder, which hides every sibling command in that folder.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && head -20 .skilled/commands/create/skill.md; echo \\\"=== readme cmd\\\"; head -12 .skilled/commands/create/readme.md; echo \\\"=== g5\\\"; cat specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt 2>/dev/null | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550622011,"end":1794550622268}}}}
