anscript records, so the code only marks a run as capped.\n1137:  *\n1138:  * A run that cannot be scored is never dropped: it comes back with the one reason\n1139:  * the summary counts apart from its denominators, so an arm that produced no\n1140:  * transcript reads as unscored rather than as a rate over the runs that survived.\n1141:  *\n1142:  * @param {object} line - One line of a run log.\n1143:  * @param {Map<string, object>} labels - The corpus labels, keyed by row id.\n1144:  * @returns {Promise<{scored: false, reason: string}\n1145:  *   | {scored: true, capped: boolean, startRow: boolean, started: boolean,\n1146:  *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offerSeen: boolean,\n1147:  *      commandState: string|null, briefDelivered: boolean|'unknown',\n1148:  *      wrote: boolean, policy: string|null, unsafe: boolean, commandLines: number,\n1149:  *      repeated: number, loop: boolean|null}>}\n1150:  */\n1151: async function scoreRun(line, labels) {\n1152:   const rowId = rowIdOf(line);\n1153:   if (rowId === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'no_row_id' };\n1154: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1155]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs, lines 1110-1154\n1110: // A command reported more than once in one session is the defect the\n1111: // once-per-command clause prevents, so this counts commands rather than lines.\n1112: function repeatedCommands(lines) {\n1113:   const counts = new Map();\n1114:   for (const line of lines) counts.set(line.command, line.count);\n1115:   return [...counts.values()].filter((count) => count > 1).length;\n1116: }\n1117: \n1118: // The offer a turn received lives on its run line, because the hook's head is not\n1119: // part of the session the reader loads. A line written before that field existed\n1120: // has no answer, so a missing key is counted apart from an offer that named another\n1121: // command instead of being read as a refusal.\n1122: function offerOf(line, label) {\n1123:   const hasOffer = Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(line, 'offeredCommand');\n1124:   const wanted = commandParts(label.expected_command);\n1125:   return {\n1126:     offered: hasOffer && wanted !== null && namesCommand(line.offeredCommand, wanted),\n1127:     offerFieldAbsent: !hasOffer,\n1128:   };\n1129: }\n1130: \n1131: /**\n1132:  * Score one run log line against the row its turn answered.\n1133:  *\n1134:  * A run is scored whenever its session loads, whatever exit the turn ended with.\n1135:  * The exit code never decides a score, because a turn the cap stopped still did\n1136:  * the work its transcript records, so the code only marks a run as capped.\n1137:  *\n1138:  * A run that cannot be scored is never dropped: it comes back with the one reason\n1139:  * the summary counts apart from its denominators, so an arm that produced no\n1140:  * transcript reads as unscored rather than as a rate over the runs that survived.\n1141:  *\n1142:  * @param {object} line - One line of a run log.\n1143:  * @param {Map<string, object>} labels - The corpus labels, keyed by row id.\n1144:  * @returns {Promise<{scored: false, reason: string}\n1145:  *   | {scored: true, capped: boolean, startRow: boolean, started: boolean,\n1146:  *      offered: boolean, offerFieldAbsent: boolean, offerSeen: boolean,\n1147:  *      commandState: string|null, briefDelivered: boolean|'unknown',\n1148:  *      wrote: boolean, policy: string|null, unsafe: boolean, commandLines: number,\n1149:  *      repeated: number, loop: boolean|null}>}\n1150:  */\n1151: async function scoreRun(line, labels) {\n1152:   const rowId = rowIdOf(line);\n1153:   if (rowId === null) return { scored: false, reason: 'no_row_id' };\n1154: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1155]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"exec