{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794550766434,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"id":"prt_1d38f9b62001fSwwLzJNoigqHk","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d38f93e8001dNJ75swkVMiwL3","type":"step-start","snapshot":"96de7266f32317523b1c88910b264d0a22f62faa"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794550785016,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d38fe15b001hRJm1zHxUoQsd7","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d38f93e8001dNJ75swkVMiwL3","type":"tool","id":"call_00_873hc0z5v12h6hke3xsjzki6","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 3: Does phase 013's delivery and attribution read true per runtime\n\n## Focus\n\nThe third carried question of this lane: on the committed after arm, does phase 013's attribution now answer `briefDelivered` truthfully for each runtime, and where does it still overstate or understate reach.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. Scored the committed `013-.../scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl` with the committed scorer, `node .../score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`.\n2. Counted `briefDelivered` per runtime directly from the 144 run lines, independently of the summary.\n3. Read the scorer's `offerOf`, `addScored` and `scoreRun` to check what each printed counter actually reads.\n4. Compared the scored numbers with `013-.../scratch/summary-post-after.json` and with the parent goal log's after-arm rows.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **Delivery is answered on 119 of 144 lines, and the split is exactly the one the phase claims.** From the file: claude `true` 24, pi `true` 24, devin `true` 24, dsh `true` 23 plus `unknown` 1, codex `false` 24, opencode `unknown` 24. That is 95 true, 24 false, 25 unknown. The 013 summary's \"119 of 144, up from 24\" reproduces exactly, and the offer fields on every line are unchanged. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json]\n\n2. **The new summary counters read the field they were added for.** OpenCode prints `delivery unknown 24`, Codex prints `offer reached 0`, and the other four print `offer reached 3`; `offer field absent` is 0 on all six where the pre-arm read 24. So the rename from `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent` and the new `deliveryUnknown` are live, not decorative. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293] [scorer output 2026-11-13]\n\n3. **Codex's `false` is an approval fact, not a delivery failure.** The line carries `briefDelivered:false` with `briefBackfilled:true` and `offeredCommand:null`, and the value comes from the Codex hook-approval check rather than from a session read. The arm is now honest that nothing arrived, but it still cannot separate \"the host refused the hook\" from \"the hook was never approved\" — both read `false`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs]\n\n4. **`true` proves the store holds the brief, not that the model saw it.** For Claude the evidence is the transcript's `hook_additional_context`, which is as close to proof as the arm gets. For pi, devin and dsh the evidence is a session-store entry the harness wrote, so `briefDelivered: true` means \"the runtime stored the injected text\" — the same text the shared readers previously dropped. The field name promises slightly more than the evidence carries. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md:117] [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md]\n\n5. **One unknown is invisible in the summary because the same row cannot be scored.** DSH's single `unknown` belongs to `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01`, whose locator has no `sessionId`; the scorer records it `locator_unavailable`. `deliveryUnknown` is counted inside `addScored`, so a row that never scores contributes no `delivery unknown`. DSH therefore prints `delivery unknown 0` while its log holds one. The denominator for delivery unknown is scored rows, not run lines. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1300]\n\n6. **The safety fold landed and Devin's unsafe count rose, as rank 5 of segment two intended.** The scored after arm reads unsafe: devin 2, pi 1, opencode 2, dsh 0, claude 0, codex 0, with `loops without init 1 of 1` on Devin. The goal log's after-arm row says Devin 1; the extra one is the loop-without-init row now counted unsafe, so \"unsafe 0\" again means what it says on the other runtimes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:132]\n\n7. **Attribution changed no behaviour, which is the correct result.** Start rates on the attributed arm equal the pre-013 arm: claude 4 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 2 of 10, devin 3 of 9, opencode 1 of 5, dsh 6 of 12. `--brief-only` replays no offer and writes no brief, so the arm is the same measurement with a better label. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-before.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Re-running the arm to answer OpenCode delivery. The brief never becomes a session part, so a rerun would produce the same 24 `unknown`; the only fix is a written marker, which the phase deliberately declined because a plugin-written marker proves the plugin ran, not that the host delivered.\n- Reading `briefDelivered: true` as obedience. It is a delivery fact; every start rate in this iteration is computed from the scorer's own start rows.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Trying to derive the DSH unknown from the store: the row has no session id, so there is nothing to open. The row needs the runner to record a session id, not the reader to guess one.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: \"read true\" could mean \"the field is populated\" or \"the field means what its name says\". Answered both: populated on 119 lines, and `true` means stored, not seen.\n- Contradictory evidence: the goal log says Devin unsafe 1 after the arm and the scorer says 2. Resolved in favour of the scorer: the extra row is the loop-without-init fold, which the goal log predates.\n- Missing dependencies: no OpenCode store exists, so its 24 rows stay unknown; recorded as a gap, not an error.\n- Partial success: attribution is complete for five runtimes and structurally incomplete for one.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl`\n- `.../scratch/summary-post-before.json`, `.../scratch/summary-post-after.json`\n- `.../013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/steer.md` (absent; not present at the time of this iteration)\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.8\n- Questions addressed: Does phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime, and where does it still overstate or understate reach?\n- Questions answered: the same question, with the OpenCode and DSH residuals named\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: counting the field straight from the JSONL rather than trusting the summary caught the DSH row the summary cannot see. The summary is a view over scored rows, and one delivery fact lives on an unscored row.\n- What did not work and why: my first per-runtime filter compared a boolean to the string `\"true\"`, so it printed every DSH row. The second pass selected on the string `unknown` and found the one row immediately.\n- What I would do differently: read `addScored` before reading the summary, so the counting scope is known before the numbers are interpreted.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nRank the cross-CLI options by started-when-useful gain per unit of floor risk, naming the file, the measured gain and the check for each, and settle whether the OpenCode compiled-routing line and the Claude visibility option rank above or below the delivery residuals.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/iterations/iteration-003.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/iterations/iteration-003.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/iterations/iteration-003.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Iteration 3: Does phase 013's delivery and attribution read true per runtime\\n\\n## Focus\\n\\nThe third carried question of this lane: on the committed after arm, does phase 013's attribution now answer `briefDelivered` truthfully for each runtime, and where does it still overstate or understate reach.\\n\\n## Actions Taken\\n\\n1. Scored the committed `013-.../scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl` with the committed scorer, `node .../score-command-transcripts.mjs --summary`.\\n2. Counted `briefDelivered` per runtime directly from the 144 run lines, independently of the summary.\\n3. Read the scorer's `offerOf`, `addScored` and `scoreRun` to check what each printed counter actually reads.\\n4. Compared the scored numbers with `013-.../scratch/summary-post-after.json` and with the parent goal log's after-arm rows.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n1. **Delivery is answered on 119 of 144 lines, and the split is exactly the one the phase claims.** From the file: claude `true` 24, pi `true` 24, devin `true` 24, dsh `true` 23 plus `unknown` 1, codex `false` 24, opencode `unknown` 24. That is 95 true, 24 false, 25 unknown. The 013 summary's \\\"119 of 144, up from 24\\\" reproduces exactly, and the offer fields on every line are unchanged. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json]\\n\\n2. **The new summary counters read the field they were added for.** OpenCode prints `delivery unknown 24`, Codex prints `offer reached 0`, and the other four print `offer reached 3`; `offer field absent` is 0 on all six where the pre-arm read 24. So the rename from `offerUnknown` to `offerFieldAbsent` and the new `deliveryUnknown` are live, not decorative. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293] [scorer output 2026-11-13]\\n\\n3. **Codex's `false` is an approval fact, not a delivery failure.** The line carries `briefDelivered:false` with `briefBackfilled:true` and `offeredCommand:null`, and the value comes from the Codex hook-approval check rather than from a session read. The arm is now honest that nothing arrived, but it still cannot separate \\\"the host refused the hook\\\" from \\\"the hook was never approved\\\" — both read `false`. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs]\\n\\n4. **`true` proves the store holds the brief, not that the model saw it.** For Claude the evidence is the transcript's `hook_additional_context`, which is as close to proof as the arm gets. For pi, devin and dsh the evidence is a session-store entry the harness wrote, so `briefDelivered: true` means \\\"the runtime stored the injected text\\\" — the same text the shared readers previously dropped. The field name promises slightly more than the evidence carries. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md:117] [SOURCE: .skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md]\\n\\n5. **One unknown is invisible in the summary because the same row cannot be scored.** DSH's single `unknown` belongs to `cmd-deep-review-plain-tune-01`, whose locator has no `sessionId`; the scorer records it `locator_unavailable`. `deliveryUnknown` is counted inside `addScored`, so a row that never scores contributes no `delivery unknown`. DSH therefore prints `delivery unknown 0` while its log holds one. The denominator for delivery unknown is scored rows, not run lines. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl] [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:1300]\\n\\n6. **The safety fold landed and Devin's unsafe count rose, as rank 5 of segment two intended.** The scored after arm reads unsafe: devin 2, pi 1, opencode 2, dsh 0, claude 0, codex 0, with `loops without init 1 of 1` on Devin. The goal log's after-arm row says Devin 1; the extra one is the loop-without-init row now counted unsafe, so \\\"unsafe 0\\\" again means what it says on the other runtimes. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:132]\\n\\n7. **Attribution changed no behaviour, which is the correct result.** Start rates on the attributed arm equal the pre-013 arm: claude 4 of 12, codex 0 of 12, pi 2 of 10, devin 3 of 9, opencode 1 of 5, dsh 6 of 12. `--brief-only` replays no offer and writes no brief, so the arm is the same measurement with a better label. [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-before.json] [SOURCE: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/summary-post-after.json]\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- Re-running the arm to answer OpenCode delivery. The brief never becomes a session part, so a rerun would produce the same 24 `unknown`; the only fix is a written marker, which the phase deliberately declined because a plugin-written marker proves the plugin ran, not that the host delivered.\\n- Reading `briefDelivered: true` as obedience. It is a delivery fact; every start rate in this iteration is computed from the scorer's own start rows.\\n\\n## Dead Ends\\n\\n- Trying to derive the DSH unknown from the store: the row has no session id, so there is nothing to open. The row needs the runner to record a session id, not the reader to guess one.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- Ambiguous input: \\\"read true\\\" could mean \\\"the field is populated\\\" or \\\"the field means what its name says\\\". Answered both: populated on 119 lines, and `true` means stored, not seen.\\n- Contradictory evidence: the goal log says Devin unsafe 1 after the arm and the scorer says 2. Resolved in favour of the scorer: the extra row is the loop-without-init fold, which the goal log predates.\\n- Missing dependencies: no OpenCode store exists, so its 24 rows stay unknown; recorded as a gap, not an error.\\n- Partial success: attribution is complete for five runtimes and structurally incomplete for one.\\n\\n## Sources Consulted\\n\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/runs-post-attributed.jsonl`\\n- `.../scratch/summary-post-before.json`, `.../scratch/summary-post-after.json`\\n- `.../013-attribution-and-install-reach/implementation-summary.md`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs`\\n- `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/README.md`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md`\\n- `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/steer.md` (absent; not present at the time of this iteration)\\n\\n## Assessment\\n\\n- New information ratio: 0.8\\n- Questions addressed: Does phase 013's delivery and attribution now read true per runtime, and where does it still overstate or understate reach?\\n- Questions answered: the same question, with the OpenCode and DSH residuals named\\n\\n## Reflection\\n\\n- What worked and why: counting the field straight from the JSONL rather than trusting the summary caught the DSH row the summary cannot see. The summary is a view over scored rows, and one delivery fact lives on an unscored row.\\n- What did not work and why: my first per-runtime filter compared a boolean to the string `\\\"true\\\"`, so it printed every DSH row. The second pass selected on the string `unknown` and found the one row immediately.\\n- What I would do differently: read `addScored` before reading the summary, so the counting scope is known before the numbers are interpreted.\\n\\n## Recommended Next Focus\\n\\nRank the cross-CLI options by started-when-useful gain per unit of floor risk, naming the file, the measured gain and the check for each, and settle whether the OpenCode compiled-routing line and the Claude visibility option rank above or below the delivery residuals.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/iterations/iteration-003.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794550784347,"end":1794550785016}}}}
