{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794551103535,"sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d394ba7b001YBhuxmZcDTnVmE","sessionID":"ses_e2c799dd1ffeZnROszLt7sZevy","messageID":"msg_1d39490aa0013vl78FaTsajGpf","type":"tool","id":"call_00_7qlaxm1h4zz17otv511z2tq1","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && L=specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3 && Q='What does the degraded (daemon-unreachable) path lose per runtime that the live path keeps, and what is the smallest change that makes the fallback carry the same command?' && cat > \"$L/deltas/iter-005.jsonl\" <<EOF\n{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"run\":5,\"runId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\",\"lineageId\":\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\",\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"The degraded path: what it loses, who hits it, and the smallest fix\",\"findingsCount\":8,\"newInfoRatio\":0.7,\"noveltyJustification\":\"Six findings are new measurements (the reproduced degraded heads, the two corrected 012 premises, the doctor top difference, the offline route availability and the zero frequency), while the trigger conditions and the fix shape are analysis of code already read.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"$Q\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"$Q\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"starting a daemon or a second socket directory to measure the fallback live\",\"treating the 012 note as the current behaviour\"],\"focusTrack\":\"cross-cli\",\"edgeCase\":\"contradictory-evidence\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Read\",\"Write\",\"Bash\",\"Grep\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts\",\".skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/degraded-parity.json\"],\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-13T08:22:41.000Z\",\"durationMs\":560000,\"graphEvents\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-001\",\"label\":\"The degraded answer is the bare scorer plus a lossy shaper, not a degraded handler answer: the fallback spawns skill_advisor.py whose own rows say source native, then passes them through degradedRecommendations which has no attach step, so on seven probe prompts the local top equals the live top on six while every head loses command, policy and mode label.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1455\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1481\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/degraded-parity.json\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-002\",\"label\":\"The 012 note's claim that a typed command is kept does not reproduce at HEAD: for /create:readme for the utils folder the scorer top is sk-doc with no command and commandRowFor sk-doc returns undefined, so the typed branch never fires and the degraded head is Advisor: stale; use sk-doc 0.95/0.12 pass.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/degraded-parity.json\",\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/live-heads.txt:23\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-003\",\"label\":\"The 012 note's claim that a plain readme request goes to another skill no longer reproduces: the local scorer ranks sk-doc 0.95/0.12 first for write a readme for the utils folder, the same top as live, so the remaining gap is the command and policy rather than the routing.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/degraded-parity.json\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-004\",\"label\":\"Only the doctor prompt's top differs: live names the command row command-doctor-setup and prints /doctor:setup (run) while the local scorer names system-skilled-doctor with no command, a ranking difference in the bridge rows that needs an owner-to-command lookup as well as the attach step.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/scratch/degraded-parity.json\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-005\",\"label\":\"Everything the attach step needs is available with no daemon: compiled-route.cjs returns route single sk-create-readme for sk-doc plus the readme prompt, route single research for system-deep-loop plus the deep-research prompt and defer for the bare skill prompt, MODE_COMMANDS maps both to /create:readme and /deep:research, and typedCommandIn already returns /create:readme.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/bin/compiled-route.cjs\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:15\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-006\",\"label\":\"In the committed arms the degraded path was taken zero times where it could be observed: Advisor: stale appears in 0 of 107 Claude transcripts, 0 of 33 Codex session files dated 2026-11-13, 0 of 36 Pi files touched on the arm date and 0 in the DSH store, while Codex's zero is uninformative because its hooks were unapproved and OpenCode keeps no store.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-007\",\"label\":\"The trigger is narrower than no daemon: the CLI starts the daemon and waits so a cold daemon alone does not reach the fallback, and it takes a failed spawn, a crashed daemon or an unreachable socket; the Claude hook imports the CLI fallback reader and the OpenCode plugin spawns the same CLI, while whether Pi, Devin and DSH adapters inherit it is UNKNOWN.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1368\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.ts:347\"]}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"id\":\"f-iter005-008\",\"label\":\"Smallest change: call the handler's own enrichment before degradedRecommendations shapes the rows, using compiledRouteForRecommendation plus attachCommand for a hub top, typedCommandIn and typedCommandForTop for a typed prompt, MODE_COMMANDS for a defer and an owner-to-command lookup for system-skilled-doctor; measured feasibility is the offline route lookup and the expected five-of-six match is inference, with no floor risk and one local subprocess per degraded prompt.\",\"iteration\":5,\"sources\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:583\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/skill-advisor-cli.ts:1572\"]}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Starting a daemon or a second socket directory to measure the fallback live\",\"reason\":\"The same two functions can be exercised without one, and starting a second daemon is forbidden in this lane.\",\"iteration\":5}\n{\"type\":\"ruled_out\",\"direction\":\"Treating the 012 note as the current behaviour\",\"reason\":\"Two of its three claims do not reproduce at HEAD; the third, that the mode label and doctor hand-off are lost, does.\",\"iteration\":5}\nEOF\nhead -1 \"$L/deltas/iter-005.jsonl\" > \"$L/logs/iter-005-event.json\" && node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/append-mode-event.cjs --mode research --run-directory \"$L\" --event-json \"$L/logs/iter-005-event.json\" | head -2; echo \"GATEWAY_EXIT=$?\"; node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-research/scripts/reduce-state.cjs specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research --artifact-dir \"$L\" 2>&1 | grep -E \"iterationsCompleted|corruptionCount\"; echo \"=== questions\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' \"$L/deep-research-strategy.md\" | grep -c \"^\\- \\[x\\]\"; sed -n '/ANCHOR:key-questions/,/\\/ANCHOR:key-questions/p' \"$L/deep-research-strategy.md\" | grep -c \"^\\- \\[ \\]\""},"output":"{\"ok\":true,\"receipt\":{\"ledger_id\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"sequence\":6,\"event_id\":\"event-5af275f5-bf78-4391-96c1-9c3a08a04e47\",\"event_type\":\"deep-research.ledger.iteration-completed\",\"event_version\":1,\"stream_id\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"stream_sequence\":6,\"committed_at\":\"2026-11-13T06:25:03.174Z\",\"canonicalEventHash\":\"744cbb83bac56724f09414d5eda568eafbcb25dd4a2764dc8288f60d34044e83\",\"recordHash\":\"79aeca156dc767c8283c28050381b8bcfa49f3959b6c5f9bbe92f151687822f7\",\"authorizationRef\":{\"audit_ledger_id\":\"deep-research-audit-ledger\",\"audit_sequence\":7,\"audit_record_hash\":\"a06e61b45e7323b0cb2dc6b93145de80e71e14c4896b6304516252ce01cf0b2e\",\"decision_id\":\"decision-051fd65b-3d6e-4886-ac09-b9480d024fd3\",\"decision_digest\":\"cae74ccea3c8c3f419c5a9b9e052a66a205472e8121eafaa122a154760d5274d\",\"request_digest\":\"a3959be553a86b02b0be0c19221799564e2f7289d393e3a1de29a797e72a4b8e\",\"policy_digest\":\"a4b1c20c36f40aa5f6c82a50e7fb20354deda901fb7b2be8f51dc112f221c7dd\",\"authority_epoch\":1,\"fence_token\":6},\"ledgerId\":\"deep-research-ledger\",\"eventId\":\"event-5af275f5-bf7