nce.\",\"iteration\":6}\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deltas/iter-006.jsonl"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deltas/iter-006.jsonl","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deltas/iter-006.jsonl"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\\"type\\\":\\\"iteration\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"run\\\":6,\\\"runId\\\":\\\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\\\",\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\\\",\\\"lineageId\\\":\\\"fanout-cross-cli-3-1794550139177-nft9c6\\\",\\\"mode\\\":\\\"research\\\",\\\"target_agent\\\":\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"agent_definition_loaded\\\":true,\\\"resolved_route\\\":\\\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\\\",\\\"status\\\":\\\"insight\\\",\\\"focus\\\":\\\"Floor-input map and the close of question coverage\\\",\\\"findingsCount\\\":6,\\\"newInfoRatio\\\":0.3,\\\"noveltyJustification\\\":\\\"Two findings are new (the floor-input map and the unproven rank-1 assertion), three restate the ranked set against it, and one restates the (e) answer for the exact-match tick.\\\",\\\"keyQuestions\\\":[\\\"(e) Claude Code lists 32 of 44 commands because a command file named `skill.md` collapses its folder: which options keep every operator-facing command name intact, what does each cost per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), and what check proves 44 of 44?\\\"],\\\"answeredQuestions\\\":[\\\"(e) Claude Code lists 32 of 44 commands because a command file named `skill.md` collapses its folder: which options keep every operator-facing command name intact, what does each cost per runtime (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh), and what check proves 44 of 44?\\\"],\\\"ruledOut\\\":[\\\"running the floor scripts to re-measure\\\",\\\"treating the missing tick on (e) as a research gap\\\"],\\\"focusTrack\\\":\\\"floors\\\",\\\"edgeCase\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"toolsUsed\\\":[\\\"Read\\\",\\\"Write\\\",\\\"Bash\\\"],\\\"sourcesQueried\\\":[\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/floorcheck.sh\\\",\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/after.txt\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\\\",\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt\\\"],\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-13T08:29:05.000Z\\\",\\\"durationMs\\\":280000,\\\"graphEvents\\\":[]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-001\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"The floors are two capture scripts over the prompt corpus and the scorer and no ranked change is an input to either: FLOOR, TYPED and PLAIN come from capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs, EVAL from capture-scorer-eval-baseline.mjs, gated at typed recall 24 of 44, false_offer 0 of 35, false_offer_attached 0 of 35, typed combined 44 and the eval tuple at least [159,50,20,5].\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/012-plain-offer-reach/scratch/floorcheck.sh:20\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-002\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Rank 1 cannot move a floor because it changes only the Claude mirror tree, which the capture does not read, and the one residual path of adding the skill to canonical .skilled/skills was ruled out for exactly that reason.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs:200\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-003\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Rank 2 cannot move a floor because it changes only the plugin's system-prompt text: the capture calls the handler, not the plugin, and output.system entries never enter a scored run.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\".opencode/plugins/system-skill-advisor.js:1586\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-004\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Ranks 3 to 5 cannot move a floor for the same reason phase 013 was safe: they touch the behaviour runner's locator, the transcript scorer's counters and the delivery field, while the floor scripts read the handler and the scorer over the corpus, so the unsafe count and the delivery split can change without touching a pinned number.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/013-attribution-and-install-reach/scratch/after.txt\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-005\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"One assertion in the ranked set is still unproven: rank 1's generated .claude/skills/create/SKILL.md rendering as the skill create while the twelve create:* commands reappear rests on a Claude behaviour no listing in this lineage shows together, although it is the mechanism the 12 existing Claude skills already use.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/g5/result.txt\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"finding\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"f-iter006-006\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Question (e) options are settled: a generated Claude skill beside the command tree reaches 44 of 44 at zero cost on the other five runtimes, a case-only SKILL.md mirror and a nested index and a colon-named root mirror are unverified, and dropping the collapsed entry gives 43 of 44; the proving check must count command links plus the skill link and must stop certifying a skill.md folder as one without modelling the collapse.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6,\\\"sources\\\":[\\\"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/iterations/iteration-002.md\\\"]}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Running the floor scripts to re-measure\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"They write into the phase scratch directories outside this lineage; the committed after files are the evidence.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6}\\n{\\\"type\\\":\\\"ruled_out\\\",\\\"direction\\\":\\\"Treating the missing tick on (e) as a research gap\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"It is an exact-match bookkeeping difference corrected by this record, not new evidence.\\\",\\\"iteration\\\":6}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/009-ux-performance-cross-cli-research/research/lineages/cross-cli-3/deltas/iter-006.jsonl\"}"},"time":{"start":1794551171328,"end":1794551171766}}}}
